window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-24-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-24-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 24 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000070281","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"There are only 6 persons - Pradeep, Qamrun, Rahul, Saroj, Tania, and Umesh in a family. There are two married couple and three generations. Pradeep is the father of Tania. Umesh is the father of Saroj. Rahul is the brother of Saroj, who is female. Qamrun is the daughter-in-law of Tania.<br>Who is the father-in-law of Qamrun? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक परिवार में केवल 6 व्यक्ति - प्रदीप, क़मरुन, राहुल, सरोज, तानिया तथा उमेश हैं। परिवार में दो विवाहित युग्म तथा तीन पीढ़ियाँ हैं। प्रदीप, तानिया का पिता है। उमेश, सरोज का पिता है। राहुल, सरोज का भाई है, जो महिला है। क़मरुन, तानिया की पुत्रवधू है।<br>क़मरुन का ससुर कौन है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Either Pradeep or Rahul","hi":"प्रदीप या राहुल"},"2":{"en":"Umesh","hi":"उमेश"},"3":{"en":"Pradeep","hi":"प्रदीप"},"4":{"en":"Rahul","hi":"राहुल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Qamrun is the daughter-in-law of Tania, so the husband of Qamrun is the son of Tania<br>Two couples and three generations must fit the six persons, and Pradeep is the father of Tania, so Tania belongs to the second generation and her husband is Umesh, whose children are Saroj and Rahul<br>Rahul is the brother of Saroj, so Rahul is the son of Tania and Umesh and he is the husband of Qamrun<br>Now Qamrun's father-in-law is the father of her husband Rahul, that is Umesh<br><svg width=\"280\" height=\"196\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 196\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M34 85H118M34 91H118\"/><path d=\"M130 151H214M130 157H214\"/><path d=\"M124 28V55H124V78\"/><path d=\"M76 94V121H28V144\"/><path d=\"M76 94V121H124V144\"/><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Pradeep+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Pradeep+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Umesh+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Umesh+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Tania−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Tania−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Saroj−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Saroj−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Rahul+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Rahul+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Qamrun−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Qamrun−</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></g></svg><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Umesh.</b>","hi":"क़मरुन, तानिया की पुत्रवधू है, अतः क़मरुन का पति तानिया का पुत्र है<br>छह व्यक्तियों में दो युग्म तथा तीन पीढ़ियाँ होनी चाहिए, और प्रदीप तानिया का पिता है, अतः तानिया दूसरी पीढ़ी की है और उसका पति उमेश है, जिसकी संतान सरोज तथा राहुल हैं<br>राहुल सरोज का भाई है, अतः राहुल तानिया और उमेश का पुत्र है और वही क़मरुन का पति है<br>अब क़मरुन का ससुर उसके पति राहुल का पिता अर्थात् उमेश है<br><svg width=\"280\" height=\"196\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 196\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M34 85H118M34 91H118\"/><path d=\"M130 151H214M130 157H214\"/><path d=\"M124 28V55H124V78\"/><path d=\"M76 94V121H28V144\"/><path d=\"M76 94V121H124V144\"/><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Pradeep+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Pradeep+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Umesh+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Umesh+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Tania−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Tania−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Saroj−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Saroj−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Rahul+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Rahul+</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Qamrun−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Qamrun−</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></g></svg><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): उमेश है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000070282","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, two groups of letters are related by a specific pattern. Identify the same pattern and apply it to the second group to find the missing letters.<br>MONK : NLOH :: TIGER : ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में अक्षरों के दो समूह एक विशिष्ट पैटर्न से संबंधित हैं। वही पैटर्न पहचानिए और दूसरे समूह पर लागू करके लुप्त अक्षर ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>MONK : NLOH :: TIGER : ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"UJHFS"},"2":{"en":"SHFDQ"},"3":{"en":"SFFBQ"},"4":{"en":"UFHBS"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In MONK the letters change alternately by +1 and −3: M → N (+1), O → L (−3), N → O (+1), K → H (−3)<br>Applying the same alternate steps to TIGER: T → U (+1), I → F (−3), G → H (+1), E → B (−3), R → S (+1)<br>So the answer is UFHBS<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): UFHBS.</b>","hi":"MONK में अक्षर बारी-बारी से +1 तथा −3 से बदलते हैं: M → N (+1), O → L (−3), N → O (+1), K → H (−3)<br>TIGER पर वही बारी-बारी चरण लगाने से UFHBS प्राप्त होता है<br>अतः उत्तर UFHBS है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): UFHBS है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000070283","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"A city government observed that districts with expanded public parks reported lower stress-related health complaints than districts without new parks. Officials concluded that public parks directly improved residents' well-being.<br>Which of the following, if true, would most weaken the officials' conclusion? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक नगर सरकार ने देखा कि जिन जिलों में सार्वजनिक उद्यानों का विस्तार हुआ, वहाँ नए उद्यान न होने वाले जिलों की तुलना में तनाव से संबंधित स्वास्थ्य शिकायतें कम दर्ज हुईं। अधिकारियों ने निष्कर्ष निकाला कि सार्वजनिक उद्यानों ने निवासियों के स्वास्थ्य को सीधे सुधारा है।<br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा, यदि सत्य हो, अधिकारियों के निष्कर्ष को सर्वाधिक कमजोर करता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Residents living near parks frequently participate in outdoor activities.","hi":"उद्यानों के निकट रहने वाले निवासी अक्सर बाहरी गतिविधियों में भाग लेते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Districts receiving new parks also received upgraded healthcare facilities.","hi":"जिन जिलों को नए उद्यान मिले, उन्हें उन्नत स्वास्थ्य सुविधाएँ भी मिलीं।"},"3":{"en":"Public parks require substantial maintenance funding each year.","hi":"सार्वजनिक उद्यानों के लिए प्रत्येक वर्ष बड़ा रखरखाव व्यय चाहिए।"},"4":{"en":"Stress-related complaints fluctuate during seasonal changes.","hi":"तनाव संबंधी शिकायतें मौसमी परिवर्तनों के साथ घटती-बढ़ती हैं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The conclusion treats the parks as the cause of the better health reports, so the argument breaks if another change also came with the parks<br>The second statement says those same districts also received upgraded healthcare facilities, which is a different and very likely cause of fewer complaints<br>The first statement supports the conclusion, and the third and fourth are unrelated or too weak<br>So the second statement most weakens the conclusion<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Districts receiving new parks also received upgraded healthcare facilities..</b>","hi":"कथन से निष्कर्ष यह मानता है कि स्वास्थ्य रिपोर्ट बेहतर होने का कारण उद्यान हैं, अतः यदि उद्यानों के साथ कोई दूसरा परिवर्तन भी हुआ तो तर्क टूट जाता है<br>दूसरा कथन कहता है कि उन्हीं जिलों को उन्नत स्वास्थ्य सुविधाएँ भी मिलीं, जो शिकायतें कम होने का भिन्न और अत्यंत संभावित कारण है<br>पहला कथन निष्कर्ष का समर्थन करता है तथा तीसरा और चौथा असंबंधित या बहुत कमजोर हैं<br>अतः दूसरा कथन निष्कर्ष को सर्वाधिक कमजोर करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): जिन जिलों को नए उद्यान मिले, उन्हें उन्नत स्वास्थ्य सुविधाएँ भी मिलीं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000070284","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Which of the following letter-clusters will replace the question mark (?) in the given series to make it logically complete?<br>MQ, NP, OO, PN, ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा अक्षर-समूह दी गई श्रेणी को तार्किक रूप से पूर्ण करने के लिए प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर आएगा?<br>MQ, NP, OO, PN, ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QM"},"2":{"en":"RL"},"3":{"en":"RM"},"4":{"en":"SL"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The first letters M, N, O, P move one place ahead each time, so the next first letter is Q<br>The second letters Q, P, O, N move one place back each time, so the next second letter is M<br>Hence the next cluster is QM<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): QM.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर M, N, O, P प्रत्येक बार एक स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला पहला अक्षर Q है<br>दूसरे अक्षर Q, P, O, N प्रत्येक बार एक स्थान पीछे जाते हैं, अतः अगला दूसरा अक्षर M है<br>इसलिए अगला समूह QM है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): QM है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000070285","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Direction: In the question below, three statements are given, followed by two conclusions numbered I and II. You must assume everything in the statements to be true, then consider the two conclusions together and decide which of them logically follows beyond a reasonable doubt from the information given in the statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>1. All patients with Type-2 diabetes benefit from regular aerobic exercise.<br>2. Some patients with Type-2 diabetes are unable to perform aerobic exercise due to joint problems.<br>3. Dr. Roy's patient has Type-2 diabetes and no joint problems.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Dr. Roy's patient benefits from regular aerobic exercise.<br>II. All patients with Type-2 diabetes and no joint problems must perform aerobic exercise. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निर्देश: नीचे दिए प्रश्न में तीन कथन और उनके बाद I तथा II क्रमांकित दो निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों की सभी बातों को सत्य मानना है, फिर दोनों निष्कर्षों पर एक साथ विचार करके निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-सा कथनों की दी गई जानकारी से संदेह से परे तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>1. टाइप-2 मधुमेह वाले सभी रोगियों को नियमित एरोबिक व्यायाम से लाभ होता है।<br>2. टाइप-2 मधुमेह वाले कुछ रोगी जोड़ों की समस्या के कारण एरोबिक व्यायाम नहीं कर पाते।<br>3. डॉ. रॉय के रोगी को टाइप-2 मधुमेह है और जोड़ों की समस्या नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. डॉ. रॉय के रोगी को नियमित एरोबिक व्यायाम से लाभ होता है।<br>II. टाइप-2 मधुमेह वाले और जोड़ों की समस्या से रहित सभी रोगियों को एरोबिक व्यायाम अवश्य करना चाहिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both I and II follow","hi":"I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Dr. Roy's patient has Type-2 diabetes, and every such patient benefits from regular aerobic exercise, so the patient benefits from it and I follows<br>The statements only state that aerobic exercise benefits such patients; they do not say that exercise is compulsory, so II does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I follows.</b>","hi":"डॉ. रॉय के रोगी को टाइप-2 मधुमेह है और ऐसे प्रत्येक रोगी को नियमित एरोबिक व्यायाम से लाभ होता है, अतः उस रोगी को लाभ होता है और I निकलता है<br>कथन केवल यह बताते हैं कि एरोबिक व्यायाम से ऐसे रोगियों को लाभ होता है; वे यह नहीं कहते कि व्यायाम अनिवार्य है, अतः II नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000070286","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the missing number in the following series:<br>7, 7, 10, ?, 33, 57 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित श्रेणी में लुप्त संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>7, 7, 10, ?, 33, 57 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15"},"2":{"en":"18"},"3":{"en":"23"},"4":{"en":"27"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The differences between consecutive terms are 0, 3, ?, ?, ? and these differences themselves grow by the odd numbers 3, 5, 7, 9<br>With the differences 0, 3, 8, 15 and 24 the series becomes 7, 7, 10, 18, 33, 57 ✔<br>So the missing term is 18<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 18.</b>","hi":"क्रमागत पदों के अंतर 0, 3, ?, ?, ? हैं और ये अंतर स्वयं विषम संख्याओं 3, 5, 7, 9 से बढ़ते हैं<br>अंतर 0, 3, 8, 15 तथा 24 लेने पर श्रेणी 7, 7, 10, 18, 33, 57 बनती है ✔<br>अतः लुप्त पद 18 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 18 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000070287","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the missing number in the following series:<br>7, 10, 16, 28, ?, 100 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित श्रेणी में लुप्त संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>7, 10, 16, 28, ?, 100 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45"},"2":{"en":"48"},"3":{"en":"50"},"4":{"en":"52"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Each term is obtained by doubling the previous term and subtracting 4, 4, 4 and so on: 7 × 2 − 4 = 10, 10 × 2 − 4 = 16, 16 × 2 − 4 = 28<br>Next term = 28 × 2 − 4 = 56 − 4 = 52 and 52 × 2 − 4 = 104 − 4 = 100 ✔<br>So the missing number is 52<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 52.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद पिछले पद का दुगुना करके 4 घटाने से प्राप्त होता है: 7 × 2 − 4 = 10, 10 × 2 − 4 = 16, 16 × 2 − 4 = 28<br>अगला पद = 28 × 2 − 4 = 56 − 4 = 52 तथा 52 × 2 − 4 = 104 − 4 = 100 ✔<br>अतः लुप्त संख्या 52 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 52 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000070288","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Select the odd number pair from the given alternatives. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए विकल्पों में से विषम संख्या-युग्म चुनिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"56, 3192"},"2":{"en":"42, 1806"},"3":{"en":"25, 650"},"4":{"en":"18, 344"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In the first three pairs the second number equals the first number multiplied by the number just below it: 56 × 57 = 3192 ✔, 42 × 43 = 1806 ✔ and 25 × 26 = 650 ✔<br>For the last pair, 18 × 19 = 342, not 344 ✘<br>So 18, 344 is the odd pair<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 18, 344.</b>","hi":"पहले तीन युग्मों में दूसरी संख्या पहली संख्या को उससे ठीक नीचे की संख्या से गुणा करने पर मिलती है: 56 × 57 = 3192 ✔, 42 × 43 = 1806 ✔ तथा 25 × 26 = 650 ✔<br>अंतिम युग्म के लिए 18 × 19 = 342 है, 344 नहीं ✘<br>अतः 18, 344 विषम युग्म है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 18, 344 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000070289","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"Each of the six letters G, A, N, I, M, E is assigned a number from 1 to 6. Choose the sequence of numbers that arranges these letters into a meaningful English word. Each number must be used exactly once.<br>G-1, A-2, N-3, I-4, M-5, E-6 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"छह अक्षरों G, A, N, I, M, E में से प्रत्येक को 1 से 6 तक एक संख्या दी गई है। वह संख्या-क्रम चुनिए जो इन अक्षरों को एक अर्थपूर्ण अंग्रेज़ी शब्द में व्यवस्थित करता है। प्रत्येक संख्या का प्रयोग ठीक एक बार होना चाहिए।<br>G-1, A-2, N-3, I-4, M-5, E-6 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1, 2, 4, 3, 6, 5"},"2":{"en":"6, 3, 4, 1, 5, 2"},"3":{"en":"5, 2, 1, 4, 3, 6"},"4":{"en":"2, 5, 1, 4, 3, 6"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The numbers 6, 3, 4, 1, 5 and 2 give the letters E, N, I, G, M and A<br>Read in this order they form the word ENIGMA, which is a meaningful English word and uses each letter once<br>No other given sequence makes a word<br>So the second sequence is the answer<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 6, 3, 4, 1, 5, 2.</b>","hi":"संख्या 6, 3, 4, 1, 5 तथा 2 से अक्षर E, N, I, G, M तथा A प्राप्त होते हैं<br>इस क्रम में पढ़ने पर शब्द ENIGMA बनता है, जो अर्थपूर्ण अंग्रेज़ी शब्द है और प्रत्येक अक्षर एक बार प्रयुक्त होता है<br>कोई अन्य दिया गया क्रम शब्द नहीं बनाता<br>अतः दूसरा क्रम उत्तर है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 6, 3, 4, 1, 5, 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000070290","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">22</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">32</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">21</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">22</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">32</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">21</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"5"},"3":{"en":"8"},"4":{"en":"7"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In every column the third number equals the first number plus twice the second number: 12 + 2 × 5 = 22 ✔ and 16 + 2 × 8 = 32 ✔<br>In the third column the same rule gives 5 + 2 × 8 = 21 ✔<br>So the missing number is 8<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 8.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक स्तंभ में तीसरी संख्या पहली संख्या तथा दूसरी संख्या के दुगुने के योग के बराबर है: 12 + 2 × 5 = 22 ✔ तथा 16 + 2 × 8 = 32 ✔<br>तीसरे स्तंभ में वही नियम 5 + 2 × 8 = 21 देता है ✔<br>अतः लुप्त संख्या 8 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000070291","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"By interchanging the given two signs, which of the following equations will be correct?<br><b>Signs: + and -</b><br>I. 15 − 3 + 2 × 4 = 14<br>II. 20 + 10 − 5 × 3 = 25 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए दो चिह्नों को परस्पर बदलने पर निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा समीकरण सही होगा?<br><b>चिह्न: + तथा -</b><br>I. 15 − 3 + 2 × 4 = 14<br>II. 20 + 10 − 5 × 3 = 25 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I","hi":"केवल I"},"2":{"en":"Only II","hi":"केवल II"},"3":{"en":"Both I and II","hi":"I और II दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither I nor II","hi":"न तो I और न ही II"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Interchanging + and − turns equation I into 15 + 3 − 2 × 4 = 15 + 3 − 8 = 10, which is not 14 ✘<br>Equation II becomes 20 − 10 + 5 × 3 = 20 − 10 + 15 = 25 ✔<br>So only the second equation is correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only II.</b>","hi":"+ और − बदलने पर समीकरण I बनता है 15 + 3 − 2 × 4 = 15 + 3 − 8 = 10, जो 14 नहीं है ✘<br>समीकरण II बनता है 20 − 10 + 5 × 3 = 20 − 10 + 15 = 25 ✔<br>अतः केवल दूसरा समीकरण सही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल II है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000070292","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option which is exactly similar to: 19-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प को चुनिए जो ठीक इसके समान है: 19-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"19-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703"},"2":{"en":"19-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai 400703"},"3":{"en":"09-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703"},"4":{"en":"19-09-2025, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The given address has the date 19-09-2026, the plot number 54/3 and the pin code 400703 joined to the city by a hyphen<br>The second option changes the hyphen before 400703 into a space, the third option changes the date to 09-09 and the fourth option changes the year to 2025<br>Only the first option matches the given address character for character<br>Hence the first option is exactly similar<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 19-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703.</b>","hi":"दिए गए पते में तिथि 19-09-2026, भूखंड संख्या 54/3 तथा पिन कोड 400703 है और पिन कोड शहर से हाइफ़न द्वारा जुड़ा है<br>दूसरे विकल्प में 400703 से पहले का हाइफ़न स्थान बन गया है, तीसरे विकल्प में तिथि 09-09 है तथा चौथे विकल्प में वर्ष 2025 है<br>केवल पहला विकल्प दिए गए पते से अक्षरशः मेल खाता है<br>अतः पहला विकल्प ठीक इसके समान है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 19-09-2026, 54/3, Palm Beach Road, Vashi, Navi Mumbai-400703 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000070293","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Since last year, the sales of laptop computers of company X have significantly increased.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. The sale of laptop computers of other companies has decreased.<br>II. The sale of laptop computers of company X was significantly lower than that of other companies in the past. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-सा कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>पिछले वर्ष से कंपनी X के लैपटॉप कंप्यूटरों की बिक्री में उल्लेखनीय वृद्धि हुई है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. अन्य कंपनियों के लैपटॉप कंप्यूटरों की बिक्री घटी है।<br>II. पहले कंपनी X के लैपटॉप कंप्यूटरों की बिक्री अन्य कंपनियों की तुलना में उल्लेखनीय रूप से कम थी। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।"},"3":{"en":"Both Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement only tells about the rise in the sales of company X, and a rise there does not mean that the sales of other companies have fallen, so I does not follow<br>It also says nothing about how company X's sales compared with other companies in the past, so II does not follow<br>Hence neither inference follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows..</b>","hi":"कथन केवल कंपनी X की बिक्री में वृद्धि बताता है, और उससे यह नहीं निकलता कि अन्य कंपनियों की बिक्री घटी है, अतः I नहीं निकलता<br>यह भी नहीं कहा गया कि पहले कंपनी X की बिक्री अन्य कंपनियों की तुलना में कैसी थी, अतः II भी नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए कोई भी निष्कर्ष नहीं निकलता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000070294","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The government has introduced several schemes to support small and medium enterprises.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. The government is trying to promote small businesses.<br>II. All small businesses are currently profitable. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सरकार ने लघु और मध्यम उद्यमों को सहयोग देने के लिए कई योजनाएँ शुरू की हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सरकार लघु व्यवसायों को बढ़ावा देने का प्रयास कर रही है।<br>II. सभी लघु व्यवसाय वर्तमान में लाभप्रद हैं। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Schemes to support small and medium enterprises show that the government wants to help such businesses grow, so conclusion I follows<br>Nothing in the statement says that all small businesses are making a profit, so conclusion II does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only Conclusion I follows.</b>","hi":"लघु और मध्यम उद्यमों को सहयोग देने की योजनाएँ दर्शाती हैं कि सरकार ऐसे व्यवसायों को बढ़ावा देना चाहती है, अतः निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br>कथन में कहीं नहीं कहा गया कि सभी लघु व्यवसाय लाभ कमा रहे हैं, अतः निष्कर्ष II नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000070295","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"In the following question a statement is given followed by some assumptions. Read the assumptions carefully and choose the appropriate option.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A retail chain is launching a new line of eco-friendly products and investing significantly in advertisements. To meet the promotional costs, it plans to close some underperforming outlets and raise capital from investors.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Customers may be interested in eco-friendly products.<br>II. Investors will definitely invest in the company. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ अवधारणाएँ दी गई हैं। अवधारणाओं को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक रिटेल श्रृंखला पर्यावरण-अनुकूल उत्पादों की नई श्रेणी शुरू कर रही है और विज्ञापनों में बड़ा निवेश कर रही है। प्रचार लागत की पूर्ति के लिए वह कुछ कम प्रदर्शन वाले आउटलेट बंद करने तथा निवेशकों से पूँजी जुटाने की योजना बना रही है।<br><b>अवधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. ग्राहकों की पर्यावरण-अनुकूल उत्पादों में रुचि हो सकती है।<br>II. निवेशक निश्चित रूप से कंपनी में निवेश करेंगे। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I is implicit.","hi":"केवल I निहित है।"},"2":{"en":"Only II is implicit.","hi":"केवल II निहित है।"},"3":{"en":"Neither I nor II is implicit.","hi":"न तो I और न ही II निहित है।"},"4":{"en":"Both I and II are implicit.","hi":"I और II दोनों निहित हैं।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A company launches a product line and spends heavily on its advertisements only if it believes that buyers will want the product, so I is implicit<br>Planning to raise capital does not mean that investors are certain to invest; the word definitely makes II too strong, so it is not implicit<br>Hence only assumption I is implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I is implicit..</b>","hi":"कोई कंपनी उत्पाद श्रेणी तभी शुरू करती है और उसके विज्ञापनों पर बड़ा व्यय करती है जब उसे विश्वास हो कि खरीदार उत्पाद चाहेंगे, अतः I निहित है<br>पूँजी जुटाने की योजना का अर्थ यह नहीं कि निवेशक निश्चित रूप से निवेश करेंगे; 'निश्चित रूप से' शब्द II को अत्यधिक दृढ़ बना देता है, अतः वह निहित नहीं है<br>इसलिए केवल अवधारणा I निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I निहित है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000070296","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If '&#9733;' means +, '&#9651;' means −, '&#9670;' means ×, and 'o' means ÷, find [(81 o 3) &#9670; (6 &#9733; 9)] &#9651; [(14 &#9670; 3) &#9733; (56 o 7)]. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि '&#9733;' का अर्थ +, '&#9651;' का अर्थ −, '&#9670;' का अर्थ × तथा 'o' का अर्थ ÷ है, तो ज्ञात कीजिए: [(81 o 3) &#9670; (6 &#9733; 9)] &#9651; [(14 &#9670; 3) &#9733; (56 o 7)]। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"154"},"2":{"en":"256"},"3":{"en":"355"},"4":{"en":"476"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"81 o 3 = 81 ÷ 3 = 27 and 6 &#9733; 9 = 6 + 9 = 15, so the first bracket is 27 × 15 = 405<br>14 &#9670; 3 = 14 × 3 = 42 and 56 o 7 = 56 ÷ 7 = 8, so the second bracket is 42 + 8 = 50<br>The whole expression is 405 − 50 = 355<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 355.</b>","hi":"81 o 3 = 81 ÷ 3 = 27 तथा 6 &#9733; 9 = 6 + 9 = 15, अतः पहला कोष्ठक 27 × 15 = 405 है<br>14 &#9670; 3 = 14 × 3 = 42 तथा 56 o 7 = 56 ÷ 7 = 8, अतः दूसरा कोष्ठक 42 + 8 = 50 है<br>पूरा व्यंजक 405 − 50 = 355 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 355 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000070297","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Many organisations are adopting AI-based automation tools to improve efficiency, although some workers fear job displacement.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. AI adoption can create concerns among employees regarding job security.<br>II. Automation always reduces the total number of jobs in an economy.<br>III. Organisations aim to improve efficiency through AI implementation. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-सा कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कई संगठन दक्षता सुधारने के लिए एआई आधारित स्वचालन उपकरण अपना रहे हैं, यद्यपि कुछ कर्मचारी नौकरी छूटने की आशंका रखते हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. एआई अपनाने से कर्मचारियों में नौकरी की सुरक्षा को लेकर चिंता उत्पन्न हो सकती है।<br>II. स्वचालन सदैव अर्थव्यवस्था में कुल नौकरियों की संख्या घटा देता है।<br>III. संगठन एआई लागू करने से दक्षता सुधारना चाहते हैं। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I और II निकलते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inferences II and III follow.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II और III निकलते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Only Inferences I and III follow.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I और III निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"All Inferences follow.","hi":"सभी निष्कर्ष निकलते हैं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The statement itself says that some workers fear job displacement, so concern about job security does arise and I follows<br>It also says that the tools are adopted to improve efficiency, so III follows<br>Nothing is said about the total number of jobs in the whole economy, so the word always makes II too broad and it does not follow<br>Hence only inferences I and III follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only Inferences I and III follow..</b>","hi":"कथन स्वयं कहता है कि कुछ कर्मचारी नौकरी छूटने की आशंका रखते हैं, अतः नौकरी की सुरक्षा की चिंता उत्पन्न होती है और I निकलता है<br>यह भी कहा गया है कि दक्षता सुधारने के लिए ये उपकरण अपनाए जा रहे हैं, अतः III निकलता है<br>पूरी अर्थव्यवस्था में कुल नौकरियों की संख्या के बारे में कुछ नहीं कहा गया, अतः 'सदैव' शब्द II को अत्यधिक व्यापक बना देता है और वह नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I और III निकलते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल निष्कर्ष I और III निकलते हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000070298","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Course of Action","question":{"en":"During a high-stakes department meeting, a relatively new employee who already struggles with professional confidence presents an incorrect data point that heavily distorts an important strategic discussion. The error is critical to operations and must be corrected immediately to prevent a flawed decision.<br>What course of action by the meeting leader demonstrates the highest level of emotional intelligence (EQ)? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक अत्यंत महत्वपूर्ण विभागीय बैठक में एक अपेक्षाकृत नया कर्मचारी, जो पहले से ही पेशेवर आत्मविश्वास की समस्या से जूझ रहा है, एक गलत आँकड़ा प्रस्तुत करता है जो महत्वपूर्ण रणनीतिक चर्चा को बुरी तरह विकृत कर देता है। यह त्रुटि परिचालन के लिए गंभीर है और गलत निर्णय रोकने के लिए तुरंत सुधारी जानी चाहिए।<br>बैठक के नेतृत्वकर्ता की कौन-सी कार्यवाही भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता (EQ) का उच्चतम स्तर दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Intervene politely to correct the error neutrally, focus strictly on facts, and follow up supportively in private.","hi":"विनम्रता से हस्तक्षेप करके त्रुटि को तटस्थ रूप से सुधारना, केवल तथ्यों पर ध्यान देना और बाद में निजी रूप से सहयोगात्मक चर्चा करना।"},"2":{"en":"Ignore the mistake entirely during the meeting to shield the new employee from public embarrassment.","hi":"नए कर्मचारी को सार्वजनिक अपमान से बचाने के लिए बैठक में गलती को पूरी तरह अनदेखा कर देना।"},"3":{"en":"Interrupt publicly to dissect why they made the error, treating it as an immediate educational case study.","hi":"सार्वजनिक रूप से टोककर यह विश्लेषण करना कि उन्होंने गलती क्यों की, और उसे तत्काल शिक्षण उदाहरण बना देना।"},"4":{"en":"Have a senior teammate immediately take over the rest of the presentation to minimize project risk.","hi":"परियोजना जोखिम कम करने के लिए वरिष्ठ साथी से प्रस्तुति का शेष भाग तुरंत ले लेने को कहना।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The error is serious and must be corrected, so ignoring it is wrong, and letting someone else take over the whole presentation takes away the employee's work<br>Publicly dissecting the mistake adds shame to an already unconfident employee and does not help the discussion<br>Correcting the data calmly and objectively keeps the decision safe while the private follow-up protects the employee's confidence and helps them improve<br>So the first course of action shows the highest emotional intelligence<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Intervene politely to correct the error neutrally, focus strictly on facts, and follow up supportively in private..</b>","hi":"त्रुटि गंभीर है और उसे सुधारना आवश्यक है, अतः अनदेखा करना गलत है, तथा किसी और से पूरी प्रस्तुति ले लेने से कर्मचारी का कार्य छिन जाता है<br>सार्वजनिक रूप से गलती का विश्लेषण पहले से कम आत्मविश्वास वाले कर्मचारी में लज्जा बढ़ाता है और चर्चा में सहायक नहीं है<br>आँकड़े को शांत और वस्तुनिष्ठ ढंग से सुधारने से निर्णय सुरक्षित रहता है और निजी चर्चा कर्मचारी का आत्मविश्वास बचाते हुए उसे सुधारने में मदद करती है<br>अतः पहली कार्यवाही भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता का उच्चतम स्तर दर्शाती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): विनम्रता से हस्तक्षेप करके त्रुटि को तटस्थ रूप से सुधारना, केवल तथ्यों पर ध्यान देना और बाद में निजी रूप से सहयोगात्मक चर्चा करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000070299","section":"REASONING","topic":"Matrix","question":{"en":"Which of the following rows/columns are connected/related with each other in some way?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">21</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">45</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">24</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">60</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">75</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">33</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">90</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पंक्तियाँ/स्तंभ किसी प्रकार एक-दूसरे से संबंधित हैं?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">पंक्ति</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">21</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">45</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">24</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">60</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">75</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">33</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">90</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Columns I, III and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, III तथा IV"},"2":{"en":"Columns II, III and V","hi":"स्तंभ II, III तथा V"},"3":{"en":"Columns I, II and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, II तथा IV"},"4":{"en":"Columns II, IV and V","hi":"स्तंभ II, IV तथा V"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Column I carries 30, 45, 60, 75 and 90 in which each number is 15 more than the one above it<br>Column III carries 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6, and column IV carries 10, 15, 20, 25 and 30, where each number is 5 more than the one above it<br>In all three columns the numbers rise by a fixed step from row to row, while columns II and V do not grow by one fixed step<br>So columns I, III and IV are related to each other<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Columns I, III and IV.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ I में 30, 45, 60, 75 तथा 90 हैं जिनमें प्रत्येक संख्या अपने ऊपर की संख्या से 15 अधिक है<br>स्तंभ III में 2, 3, 4, 5 तथा 6 हैं और स्तंभ IV में 10, 15, 20, 25 तथा 30 हैं जिनमें प्रत्येक संख्या अपने ऊपर की संख्या से 5 अधिक है<br>इन तीनों स्तंभों में पंक्ति-दर-पंक्ति संख्याएँ एक निश्चित अंतर से बढ़ती हैं, जबकि स्तंभ II तथा V किसी एक निश्चित अंतर से नहीं बढ़ते<br>अतः स्तंभ I, III तथा IV परस्पर संबंधित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): स्तंभ I, III तथा IV है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000070300","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"PAINTING\" is written as \"16aiNTI14G\". How will \"LEARNING\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"PAINTING\" को \"16aiNTI14G\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"LEARNING\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12eaRNI13G"},"2":{"en":"12eARNI13G"},"3":{"en":"12eaRNI14G"},"4":{"en":"12EARNI14G"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In PAINTING the first letter P (16) and the seventh letter N (14) are written as their alphabet positions 16 and 14, and the second and third letters A and I become small letters a and i<br>The other letters N, T, I, G stay as they are, so PAINTING gives 16 a i N T I 14 G<br>In LEARNING the first letter L is 12 and the seventh letter N is 14, and the second and third letters E and A become small e and a, so the code is 12 e a R N I 14 G<br>Hence the code is 12eaRNI14G<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12eaRNI14G.</b>","hi":"PAINTING में पहला अक्षर P (16) और सातवाँ अक्षर N (14) अपने वर्णमाला स्थान 16 तथा 14 के रूप में लिखे जाते हैं और दूसरा तथा तीसरा अक्षर A और I छोटे अक्षरों a और i में बदल जाते हैं<br>शेष अक्षर N, T, I, G वैसे ही रहते हैं, अतः PAINTING से 16 a i N T I 14 G मिलता है<br>LEARNING में पहला अक्षर L का स्थान 12 तथा सातवाँ अक्षर N का स्थान 14 है, और दूसरा तथा तीसरा अक्षर E और A छोटे e और a बन जाते हैं, अतः कूट 12 e a R N I 14 G है<br>इसलिए कूट 12eaRNI14G है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12eaRNI14G है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000070301","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question two statements are given and these statements are followed by two conclusions. You have to take the given two statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the two given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Some students are players.<br>Some players are artists.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All artists are players.<br>II. Some artists are players. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दो कथन और उनके बाद दो निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। दिए गए दोनों कथनों को सत्य मानना है, भले ही वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न प्रतीत हों। निष्कर्षों को पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-सा दोनों कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कुछ विद्यार्थी खिलाड़ी हैं।<br>कुछ खिलाड़ी कलाकार हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी कलाकार खिलाड़ी हैं।<br>II. कुछ कलाकार खिलाड़ी हैं। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The second statement says that some players are artists, which by the rule of conversion also means that some artists are players, so II follows<br>The same statement does not say that every artist is a player, so the universal conclusion I does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"दूसरा कथन कहता है कि कुछ खिलाड़ी कलाकार हैं, जिसका रूपांतरण यह भी है कि कुछ कलाकार खिलाड़ी हैं, अतः II निकलता है<br>वही कथन यह नहीं कहता कि प्रत्येक कलाकार खिलाड़ी है, अतः सार्वभौमिक निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000070302","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"A software engineer discovers a critical security vulnerability in a competitor's widely-used product that could expose millions of users. Reporting it benefits the public but aids a rival firm.<br>What is the most ethical judgement? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक सॉफ़्टवेयर इंजीनियर को एक प्रतिस्पर्धी कंपनी के व्यापक रूप से प्रयुक्त उत्पाद में गंभीर सुरक्षा कमजोरी मिलती है जो लाखों उपयोगकर्ताओं को उजागर कर सकती है। इसकी सूचना देना जनता के लिए लाभकारी है, परंतु प्रतिस्पर्धी कंपनी को सहायता भी देता है।<br>सर्वाधिक नैतिक निर्णय क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Exploit the vulnerability for competitive advantage.","hi":"प्रतिस्पर्धात्मक लाभ के लिए कमजोरी का दुरुपयोग करना।"},"2":{"en":"Ignore it; it is not their responsibility.","hi":"इसे अनदेखा करना; यह उनकी जिम्मेदारी नहीं है।"},"3":{"en":"Report it to the competitor through responsible disclosure norms.","hi":"उत्तरदायी प्रकटीकरण मानदंडों के माध्यम से प्रतिस्पर्धी कंपनी को इसकी सूचना देना।"},"4":{"en":"Publish it publicly to pressure the competitor to act faster.","hi":"प्रतिस्पर्धी पर दबाव बनाने के लिए इसे सार्वजनिक रूप से प्रकाशित करना।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The vulnerability puts millions of users at risk, so ignoring it or using it for competitive gain is clearly unethical<br>Publishing it openly would put users in even greater danger before a fix exists<br>Reporting it privately to the company under responsible disclosure lets the flaw be fixed quickly while protecting users and staying within professional ethics<br>So the third option is the most ethical judgement<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Report it to the competitor through responsible disclosure norms..</b>","hi":"सुरक्षा कमजोरी लाखों उपयोगकर्ताओं को जोखिम में डालती है, अतः अनदेखा करना या प्रतिस्पर्धात्मक लाभ के लिए उसका उपयोग करना स्पष्टतः अनैतिक है<br>सार्वजनिक रूप से प्रकाशित करने से समाधान आने से पहले उपयोगकर्ता और अधिक जोखिम में पड़ जाएँगे<br>उत्तरदायी प्रकटीकरण के अंतर्गत कंपनी को निजी रूप से सूचना देने से कमजोरी शीघ्र दूर होती है तथा उपयोगकर्ता सुरक्षित रहते हैं और पेशेवर नैतिकता का पालन होता है<br>अतः तीसरा विकल्प सर्वाधिक नैतिक निर्णय है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): उत्तरदायी प्रकटीकरण मानदंडों के माध्यम से प्रतिस्पर्धी कंपनी को इसकी सूचना देना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000070303","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Question: A store's exclusive refund policy states that a store-credit refund is given for items returned within 30 days of purchase without a receipt, provided the tags are attached. A cash refund requires a receipt and a return within 15 days of purchase. No other rules apply.<br>Scenario: An item is returned 20 days after purchase without a receipt, but with the tags attached. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"प्रश्न: एक दुकान की विशिष्ट रिफंड नीति कहती है कि बिना रसीद के खरीद के 30 दिनों के भीतर लौटाए गए सामान पर स्टोर-क्रेडिट रिफंड दिया जाता है, बशर्ते टैग लगे हों। नकद रिफंड के लिए रसीद तथा खरीद के 15 दिनों के भीतर वापसी आवश्यक है। कोई अन्य नियम लागू नहीं है।<br>परिदृश्य: कोई सामान खरीद के 20 दिन बाद बिना रसीद के लौटाया जाता है, परंतु टैग लगे हैं। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Cash refund","hi":"नकद रिफंड"},"2":{"en":"Store-credit refund","hi":"स्टोर-क्रेडिट रिफंड"},"3":{"en":"Refer to store manager","hi":"दुकान प्रबंधक को भेजना"},"4":{"en":"No refund given","hi":"कोई रिफंड नहीं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A cash refund needs a receipt and a return within 15 days, and here there is no receipt and the return is on the 20th day, so no cash refund is possible<br>A store-credit refund needs a return within 30 days without a receipt and the tags attached, and all three conditions are met here<br>So a store-credit refund is given<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Store-credit refund.</b>","hi":"नकद रिफंड के लिए रसीद तथा 15 दिनों के भीतर वापसी आवश्यक है, और यहाँ रसीद नहीं है और वापसी 20वें दिन हुई है, अतः नकद रिफंड संभव नहीं<br>स्टोर-क्रेडिट रिफंड के लिए बिना रसीद 30 दिनों के भीतर वापसी तथा टैग लगा होना आवश्यक है, और यहाँ तीनों शर्तें पूरी होती हैं<br>अतः स्टोर-क्रेडिट रिफंड दिया जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): स्टोर-क्रेडिट रिफंड है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000070304","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"While travelling on a bus, a passenger notices smoke coming from the area near the rear wheel. The driver appears unaware of it. What should the passenger do? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"बस में यात्रा करते समय एक यात्री देखता है कि पिछले पहिये के पास के भाग से धुआँ निकल रहा है। चालक इससे अनजान प्रतीत होता है। यात्री को क्या करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ignore it because the driver is responsible for the vehicle.","hi":"इसे अनदेखा करना क्योंकि वाहन की जिम्मेदारी चालक की है।"},"2":{"en":"Inform the driver or conductor immediately.","hi":"तुरंत चालक या कंडक्टर को सूचित करना।"},"3":{"en":"Wait until other passengers notice the smoke.","hi":"प्रतीक्षा करना कि अन्य यात्री धुआँ देख लें।"},"4":{"en":"Open the emergency exit while the bus is moving.","hi":"चलती बस में आपातकालीन द्वार खोलना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Smoke near a wheel can turn into a fire within moments, so a warning given at once allows the driver to stop the bus and check it<br>Waiting or ignoring the matter wastes the time that matters most, and opening the emergency door of a moving bus can cause an accident<br>So informing the driver or conductor immediately is the right action<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Inform the driver or conductor immediately..</b>","hi":"पहिये के पास का धुआँ कुछ ही क्षणों में आग बन सकता है, अतः तुरंत सूचना देने से चालक बस रोककर जाँच कर सकता है<br>प्रतीक्षा करने या अनदेखा करने से सबसे महत्वपूर्ण समय नष्ट होता है, तथा चलती बस का आपातकालीन द्वार खोलने से दुर्घटना हो सकती है<br>अतः तुरंत चालक या कंडक्टर को सूचित करना सही कार्य है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): तुरंत चालक या कंडक्टर को सूचित करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000070305","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Identify the odd one out in the following sequence:<br>2A, 4C, 6E, 8G, 10I, 12K, 14N [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित अनुक्रम में विषम पद पहचानिए:<br>2A, 4C, 6E, 8G, 10I, 12K, 14N [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6E"},"2":{"en":"14N"},"3":{"en":"10I"},"4":{"en":"12K"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The numbers rise by 2 each time and the letters move two places ahead each time: A(1), C(3), E(5), G(7), I(9), K(11) and then N(14)<br>After K the next letter should be M (13) and not N (14), so the term 14N breaks the pattern<br>Hence 14N is the odd one out<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 14N.</b>","hi":"संख्याएँ प्रत्येक बार 2 से बढ़ती हैं और अक्षर प्रत्येक बार दो स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं: A(1), C(3), E(5), G(7), I(9), K(11) और उसके बाद N(14)<br>K के बाद अगला अक्षर M (13) होना चाहिए, N (14) नहीं, अतः पद 14N पैटर्न को तोड़ता है<br>इसलिए 14N विषम पद है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 14N है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000070306","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Northern Plains and Islands","question":{"en":"Where is 'Saddle Peak', the highest mountain peak of the Andaman and Nicobar Islands, located? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"'सैडल पीक', जो अंडमान और निकोबार द्वीपसमूह की सबसे ऊँची पर्वत चोटी है, कहाँ स्थित है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Great Nicobar","hi":"ग्रेट निकोबार"},"2":{"en":"Middle Andaman","hi":"मध्य अंडमान"},"3":{"en":"Little Andaman","hi":"लिटिल अंडमान"},"4":{"en":"North Andaman","hi":"उत्तर अंडमान"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – North Andaman</b><br><b>Saddle Peak</b>, the highest point of the Andaman and Nicobar Islands at about <b>732 metres</b>, lies in <b>North Andaman</b> and is protected as the Saddle Peak National Park.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Andaman and Nicobar Islands form an arc of about <b>572 islands</b> between the Bay of Bengal and the Andaman Sea, and Port Blair is their capital.<br>• <b>Indira Point</b> on Great Nicobar is the southernmost point of India, while <b>Barren Island</b> is India's only active volcano.<br>• The islands are the extension of the <b>Arakan Yoma</b> fold mountain system and have a tropical equatorial climate with mangrove and evergreen forests.<br>• <b>Middle Andaman, Little Andaman and Great Nicobar</b> are lower in elevation than North Andaman.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because Saddle Peak is located in North Andaman.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – उत्तर अंडमान</b><br><b>सैडल पीक</b>, जो लगभग <b>732 मीटर</b> ऊँचा अंडमान और निकोबार द्वीपसमूह का सर्वोच्च बिंदु है, <b>उत्तर अंडमान</b> में स्थित है और सैडल पीक राष्ट्रीय उद्यान के रूप में संरक्षित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अंडमान और निकोबार द्वीपसमूह बंगाल की खाड़ी तथा अंडमान सागर के बीच लगभग <b>572 द्वीपों</b> की श्रृंखला है और इसकी राजधानी पोर्ट ब्लेयर है।<br>• ग्रेट निकोबार पर <b>इंदिरा पॉइंट</b> भारत का सर्वदक्षिणी बिंदु है, तथा <b>बैरन द्वीप</b> भारत का एकमात्र सक्रिय ज्वालामुखी है।<br>• ये द्वीप <b>अराकान योमा</b> वलित पर्वत प्रणाली का विस्तार हैं और यहाँ उष्णकटिबंधीय विषुवतीय जलवायु तथा मैंग्रोव एवं सदाबहार वन पाए जाते हैं।<br>• <b>मध्य अंडमान, लिटिल अंडमान तथा ग्रेट निकोबार</b> की ऊँचाई उत्तर अंडमान से कम है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि सैडल पीक उत्तर अंडमान में स्थित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000070307","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the SI unit of entropy? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से एंट्रॉपी की SI इकाई कौन-सी है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Joule","hi":"जूल"},"2":{"en":"Kelvin","hi":"केल्विन"},"3":{"en":"Joule per kelvin","hi":"जूल प्रति केल्विन"},"4":{"en":"Watt per kelvin","hi":"वाट प्रति केल्विन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Joule per kelvin</b><br>Entropy is a measure of disorder or unavailable energy of a system, and its SI unit is the <b>joule per kelvin (J/K)</b>, since entropy change is heat exchanged divided by absolute temperature.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• \\(\\Delta S = \\frac{q}{T}\\), so entropy is energy per unit temperature, measured in \\(J K^{-1}\\).<br>• The <b>second law of thermodynamics</b> states that the entropy of an isolated system never decreases.<br>• The joule is the SI unit of <b>energy or work</b>, and the kelvin is the SI unit of <b>temperature</b>.<br>• Standard entropy is measured in \\(J mol^{-1} K^{-1}\\), and entropy is a <b>state function</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the SI unit of entropy is joule per kelvin.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – जूल प्रति केल्विन</b><br>एंट्रॉपी किसी निकाय के विकार या अनुपलब्ध ऊर्जा का माप है, और इसकी SI इकाई <b>जूल प्रति केल्विन (J/K)</b> है, क्योंकि एंट्रॉपी परिवर्तन व्यय ऊष्मा को परम ताप से भाग देकर प्राप्त होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• \\(\\Delta S = \\frac{q}{T}\\), इसलिए एंट्रॉपी प्रति इकाई तापमान ऊर्जा है और \\(J K^{-1}\\) में मापी जाती है।<br>• <b>उष्मागतिकी का द्वितीय नियम</b> कहता है कि विलगित निकाय की एंट्रॉपी कभी नहीं घटती।<br>• जूल <b>ऊर्जा या कार्य</b> की SI इकाई है, तथा केल्विन <b>तापमान</b> की SI इकाई है।<br>• मानक एंट्रॉपी \\(J mol^{-1} K^{-1}\\) में मापी जाती है, और एंट्रॉपी एक <b>अवस्था फलन</b> है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि एंट्रॉपी की SI इकाई जूल प्रति केल्विन है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000070308","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Motion","question":{"en":"Which of the following statements is <b>correct</b> regarding the speed of an object in uniform circular motion? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एकसमान वृत्तीय गति में किसी वस्तु की चाल के संबंध में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन <b>सही</b> है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Always changing its value","hi":"इसका मान सदैव बदलता रहता है"},"2":{"en":"Constant throughout motion","hi":"गति के दौरान स्थिर रहता है"},"3":{"en":"Zero at all points","hi":"सभी बिंदुओं पर शून्य होता है"},"4":{"en":"Negative at all times","hi":"सदैव ऋणात्मक होता है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Constant throughout motion</b><br>In <b>uniform circular motion</b> the object moves along a circular path with <b>constant speed</b>, although its <b>velocity changes continuously</b> because the direction of motion changes at every point.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Speed is a <b>scalar</b> while velocity is a <b>vector</b>, which is why speed stays constant but velocity is not constant in this motion.<br>• A centripetal acceleration of \\(v^2/r\\) acts towards the centre, provided by tension, gravity or friction as the case may be.<br>• The direction of motion at any point is along the <b>tangent</b> to the circular path.<br>• Examples include the motion of a satellite in orbit, a stone whirled in a string and the moon around the earth.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because speed remains constant in uniform circular motion.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – गति के दौरान स्थिर रहता है</b><br><b>एकसमान वृत्तीय गति</b> में वस्तु वृत्तीय पथ पर <b>स्थिर चाल</b> से चलती है, यद्यपि उसका <b>वेग निरंतर बदलता रहता है</b>, क्योंकि गति की दिशा प्रत्येक बिंदु पर बदलती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• चाल <b>अदिश</b> राशि है जबकि वेग <b>सदिश</b>, इसीलिए इस गति में चाल स्थिर रहती है परंतु वेग स्थिर नहीं।<br>• \\(v^2/r\\) का अभिकेंद्रीय त्वरण केंद्र की ओर कार्य करता है, जो तनाव, गुरुत्व या घर्षण से मिलता है।<br>• किसी भी बिंदु पर गति की दिशा वृत्तीय पथ की <b>स्पर्श रेखा</b> के अनुदिश होती है।<br>• उदाहरण – कक्षा में उपग्रह की गति, धागे में घुमाया गया पत्थर तथा पृथ्वी के चारों ओर चंद्रमा।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि एकसमान वृत्तीय गति में चाल स्थिर रहती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000070309","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Supreme Court and High Court","question":{"en":"In India, which writ is issued by a higher court to prevent a lower court or tribunal from exceeding its jurisdiction? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में किस रिट का निर्गमन उच्च न्यायालय द्वारा अधीनस्थ न्यायालय या अधिकरण को अपने क्षेत्राधिकार से अधिक कार्य करने से रोकने के लिए किया जाता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Quo Warranto","hi":"अधिकार पृच्छा"},"2":{"en":"Habeas Corpus","hi":"बंदी प्रत्यक्षीकरण"},"3":{"en":"Mandamus","hi":"परमादेश"},"4":{"en":"Prohibition","hi":"प्रतिषेध"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Prohibition</b><br>The writ of <b>prohibition</b> is issued by a higher court to a lower court or tribunal to <b>prevent it from exceeding its jurisdiction</b> or acting contrary to natural justice, and it is issued while proceedings are pending.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Habeas corpus</b> is issued to produce a detained person; <b>mandamus</b> commands a public authority to perform its duty; <b>quo warranto</b> questions a person's authority to hold a public office.<br>• <b>Certiorari</b> is issued after the order is passed to quash it, whereas prohibition is <b>preventive</b> and issued before or during proceedings.<br>• Writs are available under <b>Article 32</b> by the Supreme Court and <b>Article 226</b> by the High Courts; Article 226 is wider in scope.<br>• Prohibition can be issued only against <b>judicial or quasi-judicial</b> authorities, not against administrative bodies.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the writ preventing a lower court from exceeding jurisdiction is prohibition.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – प्रतिषेध</b><br><b>प्रतिषेध (Prohibition)</b> रिट उच्च न्यायालय द्वारा अधीनस्थ न्यायालय या अधिकरण को <b>अपने क्षेत्राधिकार से अधिक कार्य करने</b> या नैसर्गिक न्याय के विरुद्ध कार्य करने से रोकने के लिए जारी की जाती है, और यह कार्यवाही लंबित रहते समय जारी होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>बंदी प्रत्यक्षीकरण</b> निरुद्ध व्यक्ति को प्रस्तुत करने के लिए, <b>परमादेश</b> लोक प्राधिकारी को कर्तव्य पालन का आदेश देने के लिए तथा <b>अधिकार पृच्छा</b> लोक पद धारण के अधिकार पर प्रश्न उठाने के लिए जारी होती है।<br>• <b>उत्प्रेषण (Certiorari)</b> आदेश पारित होने के बाद उसे रद्द करने के लिए जारी होती है, जबकि प्रतिषेध <b>निवारक</b> है और कार्यवाही से पहले या उसके दौरान जारी होती है।<br>• रिट <b>अनुच्छेद 32</b> के अंतर्गत सर्वोच्च न्यायालय तथा <b>अनुच्छेद 226</b> के अंतर्गत उच्च न्यायालय दे सकते हैं; अनुच्छेद 226 का दायरा व्यापक है।<br>• प्रतिषेध केवल <b>न्यायिक या अर्ध-न्यायिक</b> प्राधिकारियों के विरुद्ध जारी हो सकती है, प्रशासनिक निकायों के विरुद्ध नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि अधीनस्थ न्यायालय को क्षेत्राधिकार से अधिक कार्य करने से रोकने वाली रिट प्रतिषेध है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000070310","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Parliament","question":{"en":"Under the Tenth Schedule of the Constitution of India, which authority decides questions relating to the disqualification of Members of Parliament on the ground of defection? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के संविधान की दसवीं अनुसूची के अंतर्गत दलबदल के आधार पर संसद सदस्यों की निरर्हता से संबंधित प्रश्नों का निर्णय कौन-सा प्राधिकारी करता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Speaker /Chairman","hi":"अध्यक्ष / सभापति"},"2":{"en":"Chief Election / Election Commissioner","hi":"मुख्य निर्वाचन / निर्वाचन आयुक्त"},"3":{"en":"Supreme / High Court","hi":"सर्वोच्च / उच्च न्यायालय"},"4":{"en":"President / Vice President","hi":"राष्ट्रपति / उपराष्ट्रपति"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Speaker /Chairman</b><br>Under the <b>Tenth Schedule</b> (anti-defection law, added by the 52nd Amendment in 1985), the question of disqualification of a member on the ground of defection is decided by the <b>Speaker of the Lok Sabha</b> or the <b>Chairman of the Rajya Sabha</b>, and in states by the Speaker or Chairman of the House concerned.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Speaker's decision is based on the opinion of the party whip and is subject to <b>judicial review</b>, as held in <b>Kihoto Hollohan v. Zachillhu (1992)</b>.<br>• Disqualification applies to a member who voluntarily gives up party membership or votes against the party whip.<br>• A split of a legislature party (one-third) is no longer protected, but a <b>merger of two-thirds</b> of a party's members is exempt from disqualification.<br>• The Election Commission and the courts have no original power to decide defection cases; courts intervene only against the Speaker's decision.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because the Speaker or Chairman decides defection cases.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अध्यक्ष / सभापति</b><br><b>दसवीं अनुसूची</b> (दल-बदल विरोधी विधि, 1985 के 52वें संशोधन से जोड़ी गई) के अंतर्गत दल-बदल के आधार पर सदस्य की निरर्हता का प्रश्न <b>लोकसभा अध्यक्ष</b> या <b>राज्यसभा सभापति</b> तथा राज्यों में संबंधित सदन के अध्यक्ष या सभापति द्वारा तय किया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अध्यक्ष का निर्णय दल के व्हिप की सलाह पर आधारित होता है और यह <b>न्यायिक पुनरावलोकन</b> के अधीन है, जैसा <b>किहोतो होलोहन बनाम जाचिल्हू (1992)</b> में अभिनिर्धारित हुआ।<br>• निरर्हता उस सदस्य पर लागू होती है जो स्वेच्छा से दल की सदस्यता छोड़े या व्हिप के विरुद्ध मत दे।<br>• विधानमंडल दल का विभाजन (एक-तिहाई) अब संरक्षित नहीं है, परंतु दल के <b>दो-तिहाई सदस्यों का विलय</b> निरर्हता से मुक्त है।<br>• निर्वाचन आयोग तथा न्यायालयों को दल-बदल मामलों में मूल निर्णय की शक्ति नहीं है; न्यायालय केवल अध्यक्ष के निर्णय के विरुद्ध हस्तक्षेप करते हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि दल-बदल मामलों का निर्णय अध्यक्ष या सभापति करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000070311","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Moran, a well-known oil-producing area, is situated in which state of India? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मोरन, जो एक प्रसिद्ध तेल-उत्पादक क्षेत्र है, भारत के किस राज्य में स्थित है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gujarat","hi":"गुजरात"},"2":{"en":"Rajasthan","hi":"राजस्थान"},"3":{"en":"Assam","hi":"असम"},"4":{"en":"Odisha","hi":"ओडिशा"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Assam</b><br><b>Moran</b> is an oil-producing area of <b>Assam</b>, located in the upper Assam oil belt near Dibrugarh, and it is one of the state's old oil fields along with Digboi and Naharkatiya.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Assam's oil industry began with the discovery of oil at <b>Digboi in 1889</b>, and the Digboi refinery is India's oldest refinery.<br>• The main oil fields of Assam are <b>Digboi, Naharkatiya, Moran, Rudrasagar, Moran-Hugrijan and Lakwa</b>, operated by Oil India and ONGC.<br>• Assam is part of the <b>Brahmaputra valley</b> hydrocarbon basin, while the other major basins are the Cambay basin (Gujarat), Rajasthan's Barmer-Sanchor and the Krishna-Godavari basin.<br>• <b>Gujarat</b> leads in onshore oil production through the Cambay basin, but Moran is in Assam.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Moran oil field is situated in Assam.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – असम</b><br><b>मोरन</b> <b>असम</b> का तेल-उत्पादक क्षेत्र है, जो डिब्रूगढ़ के निकट ऊपरी असम की तेल पट्टी में स्थित है, और डिगबोई तथा नाहरकटिया के साथ राज्य के पुराने तेल क्षेत्रों में है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• असम का तेल उद्योग <b>1889 में डिगबोई</b> में तेल की खोज से आरंभ हुआ, और डिगबोई रिफाइनरी भारत की सबसे पुरानी रिफाइनरी है।<br>• असम के प्रमुख तेल क्षेत्र <b>डिगबोई, नाहरकटिया, मोरन, रुद्रसागर, मोरन-हुगरिजन तथा लकवा</b> हैं, जिन्हें ऑयल इंडिया तथा ONGC संचालित करते हैं।<br>• असम <b>ब्रह्मपुत्र घाटी</b> हाइड्रोकार्बन बेसिन का भाग है, जबकि अन्य प्रमुख बेसिन कैंबे बेसिन (गुजरात), राजस्थान का बाड़मेर-सांचोर तथा कृष्णा-गोदावरी बेसिन हैं।<br>• <b>गुजरात</b> कैंबे बेसिन से स्थल तेल उत्पादन में अग्रणी है, परंतु मोरन असम में है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि मोरन तेल क्षेत्र असम में स्थित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000070312","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which sport contributed the highest number of medals for India (12 medals) at the 2022 Commonwealth Games in Birmingham? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"बर्मिंघम में 2022 राष्ट्रमंडल खेलों में भारत के लिए सर्वाधिक (12) पदक किस खेल ने दिए? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Boxing","hi":"मुक्केबाजी"},"2":{"en":"Weightlifting","hi":"भारोत्तोलन"},"3":{"en":"Wrestling","hi":"कुश्ती"},"4":{"en":"Athletics","hi":"एथलेटिक्स"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Wrestling</b><br>At the <b>2022 Commonwealth Games in Birmingham</b>, <b>wrestling</b> contributed the highest number of medals for India – <b>12 medals</b>, comprising six gold, one silver and five bronze.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India finished <b>fourth</b> in the 2022 CWG medal tally with <b>61 medals</b> – 22 gold, 16 silver and 23 bronze.<br>• Wrestling was followed by <b>athletics (8 medals), boxing (7), weightlifting (10 including 3 gold) and badminton (6)</b>.<br>• India's wrestling gold medallists included <b>Bajrang Punia, Sakshi Malik, Deepak Punia, Ravi Dahiya and Naveen Kumar</b>.<br>• The 2026 Commonwealth Games are scheduled to be held in <b>Glasgow, Scotland</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because wrestling gave India the most medals, 12, at Birmingham 2022.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कुश्ती</b><br><b>बर्मिंघम में 2022 राष्ट्रमंडल खेलों</b> में भारत के लिए सर्वाधिक पदक <b>कुश्ती</b> ने दिए – <b>12 पदक</b>, जिनमें छह स्वर्ण, एक रजत तथा पाँच कांस्य थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत 2022 राष्ट्रमंडल खेलों की पदक तालिका में <b>चौथे स्थान</b> पर रहा और उसने <b>61 पदक</b> – 22 स्वर्ण, 16 रजत तथा 23 कांस्य जीते।<br>• कुश्ती के बाद <b>एथलेटिक्स (8 पदक), मुक्केबाजी (7), भारोत्तोलन (3 स्वर्ण सहित 10) तथा बैडमिंटन (6)</b> रहे।<br>• भारत के कुश्ती स्वर्ण पदक विजेताओं में <b>बजरंग पूनिया, साक्षी मलिक, दीपक पूनिया, रवि दहिया तथा नवीन कुमार</b> सम्मिलित रहे।<br>• 2026 राष्ट्रमंडल खेल <b>ग्लासगो, स्कॉटलैंड</b> में आयोजित होने हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि बर्मिंघम 2022 में कुश्ती ने भारत को सर्वाधिक 12 पदक दिए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000070313","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Which of the following pairs of festival and its corresponding State/Union Territory is <b>correctly</b> matched? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उत्सव तथा उससे संबंधित राज्य/केंद्रशासित प्रदेश के निम्नलिखित युग्मों में से कौन-सा <b>सही</b> मेल खाता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mahabodhi Festival – Kerala","hi":"महाबोधि उत्सव – केरल"},"2":{"en":"Sonam Lochar – Manipur","hi":"सोनम लोचर – मणिपुर"},"3":{"en":"Matho Nagrang – Ladakh","hi":"माथो नागरंग – लद्दाख"},"4":{"en":"Putul Samaroh – Meghalaya","hi":"पुतुल समारोह – मेघालय"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Matho Nagrang – Ladakh</b><br><b>Matho Nagrang</b> is a famous masked-dance festival of <b>Ladakh</b>, celebrated at the Matho monastery in the Tibetan calendar's first month, and the pair given in option (3) is correctly matched.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Mahabodhi Festival</b> is held at Bodh Gaya in <b>Bihar</b>, not Kerala, and marks Buddha's enlightenment.<br>• <b>Sonam Lochar</b> is the Losar new-year festival of <b>Sikkim</b> (Gurung and Tamang communities), not Manipur.<br>• <b>Putul Samaroh</b> is a puppet festival of <b>Rajasthan</b>, while Meghalaya's festivals include Wangala and Shad Suk Mynsiem.<br>• Other Ladakh festivals are <b>Hemis, Losar, Sindhu Darshan and Naropa</b>, and Kerala's main festivals are Onam and Vishu.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Matho Nagrang is correctly matched with Ladakh.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – माथो नागरंग – लद्दाख</b><br><b>माथो नागरंग</b> <b>लद्दाख</b> का प्रसिद्ध मुखौटा-नृत्य उत्सव है, जो तिब्बती पंचांग के प्रथम माह में माथो मठ में मनाया जाता है, और विकल्प (3) का युग्म सही मेल खाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>महाबोधि उत्सव</b> बोधगया, <b>बिहार</b> में होता है, केरल में नहीं, और बुद्ध के ज्ञानोदय का प्रतीक है।<br>• <b>सोनम लोचर</b> <b>सिक्किम</b> (गुरुंग तथा तमांग समुदाय) का लोसर नववर्ष उत्सव है, मणिपुर का नहीं।<br>• <b>पुतुल समारोह</b> <b>राजस्थान</b> का कठपुतली उत्सव है, जबकि मेघालय के उत्सवों में वांगला तथा शाद सुक मिनसिएम सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• लद्दाख के अन्य उत्सव <b>हेमिस, लोसर, सिंधु दर्शन तथा नारोपा</b> हैं, और केरल के प्रमुख उत्सव ओणम एवं विशु हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि माथो नागरंग लद्दाख से सही मेल खाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000070314","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"The platform in weightlifting refers to: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारोत्तोलन में 'प्लेटफॉर्म' का अर्थ है: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Judging panel","hi":"निर्णायक मंडल"},"2":{"en":"Warm-up area","hi":"वार्म-अप क्षेत्र"},"3":{"en":"Competition lifting area","hi":"प्रतिस्पर्धा में भार उठाने का क्षेत्र"},"4":{"en":"Medal podium","hi":"पदक मंच"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Competition lifting area</b><br>In weightlifting the <b>platform</b> is the <b>competition lifting area</b> – a square wooden or synthetic surface, usually <b>4 m × 4 m</b>, on which the lifter performs the snatch and the clean and jerk.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A barbell, discs, collars and chalk are the standard equipment, and the lifter must keep the barbell within the platform area.<br>• A valid lift requires the lifter to finish with the <b>barbell overhead, arms and legs fully extended and feet in line</b>.<br>• Olympic weightlifting has two lifts – the <b>snatch</b> and the <b>clean and jerk</b>, with three attempts in each.<br>• The judging panel consists of three referees, and a lift is valid with at least two white lights; the podium is the medal stand, not the platform.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the platform is the competition lifting area.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – प्रतिस्पर्धा में भार उठाने का क्षेत्र</b><br>भारोत्तोलन में <b>प्लेटफॉर्म</b> <b>प्रतिस्पर्धा में भार उठाने का क्षेत्र</b> होता है – एक वर्गाकार लकड़ी या कृत्रिम सतह, सामान्यतः <b>4 मीटर × 4 मीटर</b>, जिस पर भारोत्तोलक स्नैच तथा क्लीन एंड जर्क करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बारबेल, डिस्क, कॉलर तथा चॉक मानक उपकरण हैं, और भारोत्तोलक को बारबेल प्लेटफॉर्म क्षेत्र के भीतर ही रखनी होती है।<br>• वैध उठान के लिए भारोत्तोलक को <b>बारबेल सिर के ऊपर, हाथ-पैर पूर्णतः सीधे तथा पैर एक पंक्ति में</b> रखने होते हैं।<br>• ओलंपिक भारोत्तोलन में दो उठान हैं – <b>स्नैच</b> तथा <b>क्लीन एंड जर्क</b>, प्रत्येक में तीन प्रयास।<br>• निर्णायक मंडल में तीन रेफरी होते हैं और कम से कम दो श्वेत प्रकाश से उठान वैध होती है; पोडियम पदक मंच है, प्लेटफॉर्म नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि प्लेटफॉर्म प्रतिस्पर्धा में भार उठाने का क्षेत्र है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000070315","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Vedic Age","question":{"en":"Which archaeological absence at Bhagwanpura suggests its association with an early pre-Iron phase of Rig Vedic culture? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भगवानपुर में कौन-सी पुरातात्विक अनुपस्थिति ऋग्वैदिक संस्कृति के आरंभिक लौह-पूर्व चरण से उसके संबंध का संकेत देती है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The absence of iron objects","hi":"लोहे की वस्तुओं की अनुपस्थिति"},"2":{"en":"The complete absence of horse and cattle remains","hi":"अश्व तथा पशु अवशेषों की पूर्ण अनुपस्थिति"},"3":{"en":"The absence of Painted Grey Ware pottery","hi":"चित्रित धूसर मृदभांड (PGW) की अनुपस्थिति"},"4":{"en":"The absence of multi-roomed mud structures","hi":"बहु-कक्षीय मिट्टी संरचनाओं की अनुपस्थिति"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – The absence of iron objects</b><br>At <b>Bhagwanpura</b> (Haryana), the overlap of Painted Grey Ware with late Harappan pottery is dated to a phase in which <b>iron objects are absent</b>, suggesting an early pre-Iron phase associated with Rig Vedic culture.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Bhagwanpura, on the banks of the Saraswati in Kurukshetra district, was excavated by <b>J.P. Joshi</b> and shows a <b>Late Harappan and PGW overlap</b>.<br>• The site yielded <b>13-roomed mud structures, animal bones including those of the horse, and copper objects</b>, so options about absence of horses or mud structures are wrong.<br>• <b>Painted Grey Ware</b> is present at Bhagwanpura, marking the early Iron Age of the Ganga-Yamuna doab.<br>• The Rig Vedic period is generally dated to about <b>1500-1000 BCE</b>, before the widespread use of iron.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because the absence of iron objects marks the pre-Iron phase at Bhagwanpura.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – लोहे की वस्तुओं की अनुपस्थिति</b><br><b>भगवानपुर</b> (हरियाणा) में चित्रित धूसर मृदभांड तथा परवर्ती हड़प्पा मृदभांड का सहअस्तित्व उस चरण का है जिसमें <b>लोहे की वस्तुएँ अनुपस्थित</b> हैं, जो ऋग्वैदिक संस्कृति से जुड़े आरंभिक लौह-पूर्व चरण का संकेत देता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कुरुक्षेत्र जिले में सरस्वती नदी के तट पर स्थित भगवानपुर की खुदाई <b>जे. पी. जोशी</b> ने की और वहाँ <b>परवर्ती हड़प्पा तथा PGW का सहअस्तित्व</b> मिलता है।<br>• स्थल से <b>13 कक्षों वाली मिट्टी की संरचनाएँ, अश्व सहित पशु अस्थियाँ तथा ताम्र वस्तुएँ</b> मिलीं, इसलिए अश्व या मिट्टी संरचनाओं की अनुपस्थिति वाले विकल्प गलत हैं।<br>• भगवानपुर में <b>चित्रित धूसर मृदभांड</b> उपस्थित है, जो गंगा-यमुना दोआब के आरंभिक लौह युग का सूचक है।<br>• ऋग्वैदिक काल सामान्यतः लगभग <b>1500-1000 ईसा पूर्व</b> माना जाता है, लोहे के व्यापक उपयोग से पहले।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि भगवानपुर में लोहे की वस्तुओं की अनुपस्थिति लौह-पूर्व चरण दर्शाती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000070316","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Which seasoned legal professional continues to serve as the Solicitor General of India in 2026, representing the Union in high-profile constitutional cases? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-से अनुभवी विधि विशेषज्ञ 2026 में भारत के सॉलिसिटर जनरल के रूप में सेवारत हैं और उच्च-स्तरीय संवैधानिक मामलों में संघ का प्रतिनिधित्व करते हैं? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tushar Mehta","hi":"तुषार मेहता"},"2":{"en":"Harish Salve","hi":"हरीश साल्वे"},"3":{"en":"Mukul Rohatgi","hi":"मुकुल रोहतगी"},"4":{"en":"Vikramjit Banerjee","hi":"विक्रमजीत बनर्जी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Tushar Mehta</b><br><b>Tushar Mehta</b> continues to serve as the <b>Solicitor General of India</b> and represents the Union in major constitutional cases before the Supreme Court.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Solicitor General is the <b>second-highest law officer</b> of the Government of India after the Attorney General and is appointed by the Appointments Committee of the Cabinet.<br>• Tushar Mehta was appointed Solicitor General in <b>2018</b> and has appeared in cases such as the Article 370 matter and the electoral bonds case.<br>• <b>Harish Salve</b> and <b>Mukul Rohatgi</b> are former Attorneys General/Solicitors General, and <b>Vikramjit Banerjee</b> is a former Additional Solicitor General.<br>• The Attorney General is appointed under <b>Article 76</b>, while the Solicitor General's office is a statutory/executive post without a constitutional mention.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because Tushar Mehta is the Solicitor General of India in 2026.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – तुषार मेहता</b><br><b>तुषार मेहता (Tushar Mehta)</b> 2026 में भी <b>भारत के सॉलिसिटर जनरल</b> के रूप में सेवारत हैं और सर्वोच्च न्यायालय में प्रमुख संवैधानिक मामलों में संघ का प्रतिनिधित्व करते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सॉलिसिटर जनरल भारत सरकार का <b>महान्यायवादी के बाद दूसरा सर्वोच्च विधि अधिकारी</b> होता है और उसकी नियुक्ति मंत्रिमंडल की नियुक्ति समिति करती है।<br>• तुषार मेहता <b>2018</b> में सॉलिसिटर जनरल नियुक्त हुए और उन्होंने अनुच्छेद 370 तथा इलेक्टोरल बॉन्ड जैसे मामलों में पक्ष रखा।<br>• <b>हरीश साल्वे</b> तथा <b>मुकुल रोहतगी</b> पूर्व महान्यायवादी/सॉलिसिटर जनरल रहे हैं, और <b>विक्रमजीत बनर्जी</b> पूर्व अतिरिक्त सॉलिसिटर जनरल हैं।<br>• महान्यायवादी की नियुक्ति <b>अनुच्छेद 76</b> के अंतर्गत होती है, जबकि सॉलिसिटर जनरल का पद संविधान में उल्लिखित नहीं, सांविधिक/कार्यकारी है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि 2026 में तुषार मेहता भारत के सॉलिसिटर जनरल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000070317","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who took charge as India's Ambassador to the United States on 12 August 2024? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"12 अगस्त 2024 को किसने संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका में भारत के राजदूत का पदभार ग्रहण किया? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Vinay Mohan Kwatra","hi":"विनय मोहन क्वात्रा"},"2":{"en":"Vikram Misri","hi":"विक्रम मिस्री"},"3":{"en":"Santosh Jha","hi":"संतोष झा"},"4":{"en":"Jawed Ashraf","hi":"जावेद अशरफ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Vinay Mohan Kwatra</b><br><b>Vinay Mohan Kwatra</b>, a senior IFS officer and former Foreign Secretary, took charge as India's <b>Ambassador to the United States on 12 August 2024</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Kwatra served as <b>Foreign Secretary from 2022 to 2024</b> before his appointment to Washington, succeeding Taranjit Singh Sandhu.<br>• <b>Vikram Misri</b> is the Foreign Secretary from 2024, <b>Santosh Jha</b> is India's Ambassador to the European Union and Belgium, and <b>Jawed Ashraf</b> is India's Ambassador to France.<br>• The Indian Embassy in the USA is located in <b>Washington, D.C.</b>, and the ambassador is assisted by consulates in New York, San Francisco, Chicago, Houston and Atlanta.<br>• The External Affairs Minister is <b>S. Jaishankar</b>, and the Foreign Secretary is the senior-most civil servant of the Ministry of External Affairs.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because Vinay Mohan Kwatra took charge as Ambassador to the US on 12 August 2024.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – विनय मोहन क्वात्रा</b><br>वरिष्ठ IFS अधिकारी तथा पूर्व विदेश सचिव <b>विनय मोहन क्वात्रा (Vinay Mohan Kwatra)</b> ने <b>12 अगस्त 2024</b> को <b>संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका में भारत के राजदूत</b> का पदभार ग्रहण किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वाशिंगटन में नियुक्ति से पहले क्वात्रा <b>2022 से 2024 तक विदेश सचिव</b> रहे और उन्होंने तरनजीत सिंह संधू का स्थान लिया।<br>• <b>विक्रम मिस्री</b> 2024 से विदेश सचिव हैं, <b>संतोष झा</b> यूरोपीय संघ तथा बेल्जियम में भारत के राजदूत हैं, और <b>जावेद अशरफ</b> फ्रांस में भारत के राजदूत हैं।<br>• अमेरिका में भारतीय दूतावास <b>वाशिंगटन, डी.सी.</b> में है और राजदूत को न्यूयॉर्क, सैन फ्रांसिस्को, शिकागो, ह्यूस्टन तथा अटलांटा के वाणिज्य दूतावास सहयोग देते हैं।<br>• विदेश मंत्री <b>एस. जयशंकर</b> हैं, तथा विदेश सचिव विदेश मंत्रालय का सर्वोच्च सिविल सेवक होता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि 12 अगस्त 2024 को विनय मोहन क्वात्रा ने अमेरिका में राजदूत का पदभार ग्रहण किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000070318","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"What is the primary focus of <b>Component-C</b> under India's PM-KUSUM (Pradhan Mantri Kisan Urja Suraksha evam Utthaan Mahabhiyaan) scheme? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत की पीएम-कुसुम (प्रधानमंत्री किसान ऊर्जा सुरक्षा एवं उत्थान महाभियान) योजना के अंतर्गत <b>घटक-C</b> का मुख्य केंद्र क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Installation of 20 lakh standalone solar-powered pumps.","hi":"20 लाख स्टैंडअलोन सौर ऊर्जा चालित पंपों की स्थापना।"},"2":{"en":"Addition of 10,000 MW (Megawatt) capacity through small solar plants.","hi":"लघु सौर संयंत्रों के माध्यम से 10,000 मेगावाट क्षमता का जुड़ाव।"},"3":{"en":"Solarization of existing grid-connected agricultural pumps.","hi":"पहले से ग्रिड से जुड़े कृषि पंपों का सौरीकरण।"},"4":{"en":"Distribution of solar lanterns to rural landless households.","hi":"ग्रामीण भूमिहीन परिवारों को सौर लालटेन का वितरण।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Solarization of existing grid-connected agricultural pumps</b><br>Under <b>PM-KUSUM</b>, <b>Component-C</b> deals with the <b>solarization of existing grid-connected agricultural pumps</b>, so that farmers can use solar power for irrigation and sell surplus power to the grid.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Component-A</b> provides for setting up <b>10,000 MW of decentralised ground-mounted solar plants</b> of 500 kW to 2 MW capacity.<br>• <b>Component-B</b> supports installation of <b>20 lakh standalone solar-powered agricultural pumps</b>.<br>• The scheme was launched in <b>2019</b> by the Ministry of New and Renewable Energy, with a target of 30,800 MW of solar capacity and 35 lakh farmers benefitting.<br>• Distribution of solar lanterns is not part of PM-KUSUM, and the scheme supports the <b>Kisan Urja Suraksha</b> goal of energy security and extra income for farmers.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Component-C is about solarization of existing agricultural pumps.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पहले से ग्रिड से जुड़े कृषि पंपों का सौरीकरण।</b><br><b>पीएम-कुसुम</b> के अंतर्गत <b>घटक-C</b> <b>पहले से ग्रिड से जुड़े कृषि पंपों के सौरीकरण</b> से संबंधित है, जिससे किसान सिंचाई के लिए सौर ऊर्जा का उपयोग कर सकें और अधिशेष बिजली ग्रिड को बेच सकें।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>घटक-A</b> में 500 किलोवाट से 2 मेगावाट क्षमता के <b>10,000 मेगावाट विकेंद्रीकृत भूमि-आधारित सौर संयंत्र</b> लगाने का प्रावधान है।<br>• <b>घटक-B</b> <b>20 लाख स्टैंडअलोन सौर ऊर्जा चालित कृषि पंपों</b> की स्थापना को सहारा देता है।<br>• योजना <b>2019</b> में नवीन एवं नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा मंत्रालय द्वारा शुरू हुई, जिसका लक्ष्य 30,800 मेगावाट सौर क्षमता तथा 35 लाख किसानों को लाभ है।<br>• सौर लालटेन का वितरण पीएम-कुसुम का भाग नहीं है, और योजना किसानों की ऊर्जा सुरक्षा तथा अतिरिक्त आय के <b>किसान ऊर्जा सुरक्षा</b> लक्ष्य को सहारा देती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि घटक-C पहले से ग्रिड से जुड़े कृषि पंपों के सौरीकरण से संबंधित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000070319","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Banking","question":{"en":"The SWAMIH (Special Window for Affordable and Mid-Income Housing) Fund, established under the Ministry of Finance in India, is classified under which category of Alternative Investment Fund (AIF)? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वित्त मंत्रालय के अंतर्गत स्थापित स्वामीह (किफायती एवं मध्यम आय वर्ग आवास हेतु विशेष खिड़की) कोष को वैकल्पिक निवेश कोष (AIF) की किस श्रेणी में रखा जाता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Category-III Alternative Investment Fund (AIF)","hi":"श्रेणी-III वैकल्पिक निवेश कोष (AIF)"},"2":{"en":"Category-II Alternative Investment Fund (AIF)","hi":"श्रेणी-II वैकल्पिक निवेश कोष (AIF)"},"3":{"en":"Category-I Alternative Investment Fund (AIF)","hi":"श्रेणी-I वैकल्पिक निवेश कोष (AIF)"},"4":{"en":"Public-Private Infrastructure Fund (PIF)","hi":"सार्वजनिक-निजी अवसंरचना कोष (PIF)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Category-II Alternative Investment Fund (AIF)</b><br>The <b>SWAMIH Investment Fund</b>, set up in 2019 under the Ministry of Finance and managed by SBICAP Ventures, is registered as a <b>Category-II Alternative Investment Fund</b> that provides last-mile funding to complete stalled affordable and middle-income housing projects.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Category-I AIFs include <b>venture capital funds, SME funds, social impact funds and infrastructure funds</b>; Category-III AIFs are hedge funds that use complex trading strategies.<br>• SWAMIH gives priority funding to projects that are <b>RERA-registered, net-worth positive and close to completion</b>.<br>• The fund has sanctioned thousands of crores for lakhs of stalled housing units across India, with the government as a major contributor.<br>• AIFs are regulated by <b>SEBI (Alternative Investment Funds) Regulations, 2012</b>, and SWAMIH is a private fund pooled through government and institutional money.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because SWAMIH is a Category-II AIF.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – श्रेणी-II वैकल्पिक निवेश कोष (AIF)</b><br>2019 में वित्त मंत्रालय के अंतर्गत स्थापित तथा SBICAP वेंचर्स द्वारा प्रबंधित <b>स्वामीह निवेश कोष (SWAMIH)</b> <b>श्रेणी-II वैकल्पिक निवेश कोष</b> के रूप में पंजीकृत है, जो रुके हुए किफायती एवं मध्यम आय वर्ग के आवास परियोजनाओं को पूरा करने के लिए अंतिम-चरण वित्त देता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• श्रेणी-I AIF में <b>वेंचर कैपिटल कोष, SME कोष, सामाजिक प्रभाव कोष तथा अवसंरचना कोष</b> आते हैं; श्रेणी-III AIF हेज फंड हैं जो जटिल व्यापारिक रणनीतियाँ अपनाते हैं।<br>• स्वामीह उन परियोजनाओं को प्राथमिकता देता है जो <b>RERA-पंजीकृत, नेट-वर्थ धनात्मक तथा पूर्ण होने के निकट</b> हों।<br>• कोष ने देशभर में लाखों रुकी आवास इकाइयों के लिए हजारों करोड़ रुपये स्वीकृत किए हैं, जिसमें सरकार प्रमुख अंशदाता है।<br>• AIF <b>सेबी (वैकल्पिक निवेश कोष) विनियम, 2012</b> द्वारा नियंत्रित होते हैं, और स्वामीह सरकारी तथा संस्थागत धन से जुटाया गया निजी कोष है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि स्वामीह श्रेणी-II AIF है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000070320","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"Which port is often compared geopolitically with Chabahar Port? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भू-राजनीतिक दृष्टि से चाबहार बंदरगाह की तुलना प्रायः किस बंदरगाह से की जाती है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Jebel Ali","hi":"जेबेल अली"},"2":{"en":"Duqm","hi":"दुक़म"},"3":{"en":"Hambantota","hi":"हंबनटोटा"},"4":{"en":"Gwadar","hi":"ग्वादर"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Gwadar</b><br><b>Chabahar port</b>, developed by India in Iran, is often compared geopolitically with <b>Gwadar port</b> in Pakistan, which is developed with Chinese assistance as part of the China-Pakistan Economic Corridor.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Chabahar lies in Iran's Sistan-Baluchestan province on the Gulf of Oman and gives India access to Afghanistan and Central Asia bypassing Pakistan.<br>• India has operated the <b>Shahid Beheshti terminal</b> at Chabahar, and in 2024 India Ports Global signed a ten-year agreement to operate it.<br>• Chabahar is linked to the <b>International North-South Transport Corridor</b> and to INSTC via Iran's rail network.<br>• <b>Gwadar</b> is in Pakistan's Balochistan and is the flagship of CPEC; <b>Hambantota</b> is in Sri Lanka, <b>Duqm</b> in Oman and <b>Jebel Ali</b> in the UAE.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because Chabahar is geopolitically compared with Gwadar.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – ग्वादर</b><br>ईरान में भारत द्वारा विकसित <b>चाबहार बंदरगाह</b> की भू-राजनीतिक तुलना प्रायः पाकिस्तान के <b>ग्वादर बंदरगाह</b> से की जाती है, जिसे चीन-पाकिस्तान आर्थिक गलियारे के अंतर्गत चीनी सहायता से विकसित किया जा रहा है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• चाबहार ओमान की खाड़ी पर ईरान के सिस्तान-बलूचिस्तान प्रांत में है और यह भारत को पाकिस्तान से बचते हुए अफगानिस्तान तथा मध्य एशिया तक पहुँच देता है।<br>• भारत चाबहार के <b>शहीद बेहेश्ती टर्मिनल</b> का संचालन करता रहा है, और 2024 में इंडिया पोर्ट्स ग्लोबल ने इसके संचालन हेतु दस-वर्षीय समझौता किया।<br>• चाबहार <b>अंतरराष्ट्रीय उत्तर-दक्षिण परिवहन गलियारे</b> से तथा ईरान के रेल नेटवर्क के माध्यम से INSTC से जुड़ा है।<br>• <b>ग्वादर</b> पाकिस्तान के बलूचिस्तान में है और CPEC का प्रमुख अंग है; <b>हंबनटोटा</b> श्रीलंका, <b>दुक़म</b> ओमान तथा <b>जेबेल अली</b> संयुक्त अरब अमीरात में हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि चाबहार की भू-राजनीतिक तुलना ग्वादर से की जाती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000070321","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"Under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India, which of the following actions does not satisfy the requirement of \"good faith\"? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी कार्रवाई \"सद्भावना\" (good faith) की शर्त पूरी नहीं करती? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Acting honestly after careful verification of facts","hi":"तथ्यों के सावधान सत्यापन के पश्चात ईमानदारी से कार्य करना"},"2":{"en":"Taking a decision after exercising due care and attention","hi":"उचित सावधानी तथा ध्यान बरतते हुए निर्णय लेना"},"3":{"en":"Acting honestly but recklessly without proper inquiry","hi":"उचित जाँच के बिना ईमानदारी से परंतु लापरवाही से कार्य करना"},"4":{"en":"Believing information after reasonable investigation","hi":"उचित जाँच के पश्चात सूचना पर विश्वास करना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Acting honestly but recklessly without proper inquiry</b><br>Under the <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023</b>, a thing is done in <b>good faith</b> if it is done with <b>due care and attention</b>; acting honestly but <b>recklessly without proper inquiry</b> lacks that care and attention, so it does not satisfy the requirement of good faith.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Good faith combines <b>honesty of intention with due care and attention</b>, a test stricter than mere 'honesty' under the BNS.<br>• The definition appears in the <b>General Explanations</b> of the BNS and replaces the old Indian Penal Code requirement.<br>• The classic case <b>Vijaya v. State of Maharashtra (1963)</b> held that a person acting negligently cannot claim good faith.<br>• Good faith is a defence in several offences such as defamation, acts of judges and communication made in good faith to protect interests.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because recklessness without inquiry negates good faith.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – उचित जाँच के बिना ईमानदारी से परंतु लापरवाही से कार्य करना</b><br><b>भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023</b> के अंतर्गत कोई कार्य <b>सद्भावना</b> से किया गया तभी माना जाता है जब वह <b>उचित सावधानी तथा ध्यान</b> के साथ किया गया हो; ईमानदारी से परंतु <b>उचित जाँच के बिना लापरवाही से</b> किया गया कार्य उस सावधानी एवं ध्यान का अभाव रखता है, इसलिए वह सद्भावना की शर्त पूरी नहीं करता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सद्भावना में <b>आशय की ईमानदारी के साथ उचित सावधानी तथा ध्यान</b> दोनों आवश्यक हैं, जो BNS के अंतर्गत केवल 'ईमानदारी' से कठोर परीक्षण है।<br>• यह परिभाषा BNS के <b>सामान्य व्याख्या</b> भाग में दी गई है और पुरानी भारतीय दंड संहिता की अपेक्षा का स्थान लेती है।<br>• प्रसिद्ध मामले <b>विजया बनाम महाराष्ट्र राज्य (1963)</b> में अभिनिर्धारित हुआ कि लापरवाही से कार्य करने वाला सद्भावना का दावा नहीं कर सकता।<br>• सद्भावना विभिन्न अपराधों में प्रतिरक्षा है, जैसे मानहानि, न्यायाधीशों के कृत्य तथा हित की रक्षा हेतु सद्भावना से किया गया संचार।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि जाँच के बिना लापरवाही सद्भावना को निष्फल करती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000070322","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A tribunal consisting of three officers gives a legally binding judgement which becomes final unless appealed. Under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India, these officers would collectively be regarded as: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"तीन अधिकारियों का एक अधिकरण विधिक रूप से बाध्यकारी निर्णय देता है, जो अपील के अभाव में अंतिम होता है। भारत में भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत ये अधिकारी सामूहिक रूप से किस रूप में माने जाएँगे? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Arbitrators only","hi":"केवल मध्यस्थ"},"2":{"en":"Witnesses","hi":"साक्षी"},"3":{"en":"A court and its members as judges while acting judicially","hi":"एक न्यायालय तथा न्यायिक रूप से कार्य करते समय उसके सदस्य न्यायाधीश"},"4":{"en":"Administrative authorities with no judicial status","hi":"न्यायिक स्थिति रहित प्रशासनिक प्राधिकारी"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – A court and its members as judges while acting judicially</b><br>Under the <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023</b>, where persons are empowered to act judicially and their decision is legally binding and final unless appealed, they constitute a <b>court</b> and its members are treated as <b>judges</b> while so acting.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The definition of 'court of justice' and 'judge' in the BNS covers <b>tribunals and quasi-judicial bodies</b> that give binding decisions.<br>• Members of such bodies get the same protection for acts done in good faith as judges of a court of justice.<br>• The test is <b>the power to act judicially plus a binding, final decision</b>, not merely the name of the body.<br>• Arbitrators, witnesses and purely administrative authorities do not satisfy both conditions, so options (1), (2) and (4) are wrong.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because such officers collectively form a court and act as judges.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – एक न्यायालय तथा न्यायिक रूप से कार्य करते समय उसके सदस्य न्यायाधीश</b><br><b>भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023</b> के अंतर्गत जहाँ व्यक्तियों को न्यायिक रूप से कार्य करने की शक्ति प्राप्त है और उनका निर्णय विधिक रूप से बाध्यकारी तथा अपील के अभाव में अंतिम होता है, वहाँ वे <b>न्यायालय</b> होते हैं और ऐसा कार्य करते समय उनके सदस्य <b>न्यायाधीश</b> माने जाते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BNS में 'न्याय का न्यायालय' तथा 'न्यायाधीश' की परिभाषा में <b>अधिकरण तथा अर्ध-न्यायिक निकाय</b> सम्मिलित हैं जो बाध्यकारी निर्णय देते हैं।<br>• ऐसे निकायों के सदस्यों को सद्भावना से किए गए कृत्यों के लिए न्यायालय के न्यायाधीश के समान संरक्षण मिलता है।<br>• परीक्षण यह है – <b>न्यायिक रूप से कार्य करने की शक्ति तथा बाध्यकारी और अंतिम निर्णय</b>, केवल निकाय का नाम नहीं।<br>• मध्यस्थ, साक्षी तथा पूर्णतः प्रशासनिक प्राधिकारी दोनों शर्तें पूरी नहीं करते, इसलिए विकल्प (1), (2) तथा (4) गलत हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि ऐसे अधिकारी सामूहिक रूप से न्यायालय बनाते हैं और न्यायाधीश के रूप में कार्य करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000070323","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"Who became India's first fully blind woman Indian Administrative Service (IAS) officer by securing All India Rank 124 in the Union Public Service Commission Civil Services Examination (UPSC CSE) after losing her eyesight at the age of six? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"छह वर्ष की आयु में दृष्टि खोने के बाद संघ लोक सेवा आयोग सिविल सेवा परीक्षा (UPSC CSE) में अखिल भारतीय रैंक 124 प्राप्त करके भारत की प्रथम पूर्णतः दृष्टिबाधित महिला भारतीय प्रशासनिक सेवा (IAS) अधिकारी कौन बनीं? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Beno Zephine","hi":"बीनू ज़ेफ़ीन"},"2":{"en":"Ira Singhal","hi":"ईरा सिंघल"},"3":{"en":"Pranjal Patil","hi":"प्रांजल पाटिल"},"4":{"en":"Kiran Bedi","hi":"किरण बेदी"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Pranjal Patil</b><br><b>Pranjal Patil</b> became India's <b>first fully blind woman IAS officer</b> by securing <b>All India Rank 124</b> in the UPSC Civil Services Examination 2016, having lost her eyesight at the age of six.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• She was appointed to the <b>Kerala cadre</b> and has served as Sub-Collector of Thiruvananthapuram and as CEO of the Ulhasnagar Municipal Corporation.<br>• <b>Beno Zephine</b> was the first 100% visually impaired woman to join the <b>Indian Foreign Service</b> (2015), not the IAS.<br>• <b>Ira Singhal</b> topped the UPSC CSE 2014 and is a differently-abled officer, while <b>Kiran Bedi</b> was India's first woman IPS officer.<br>• The UPSC provides <b>scribe and extra-time facilities</b> for visually impaired candidates under its examination rules.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Pranjal Patil was the first fully blind woman IAS officer.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – प्रांजल पाटिल</b><br><b>प्रांजल पाटिल (Pranjal Patil)</b> छह वर्ष की आयु में दृष्टि खोने के बाद UPSC सिविल सेवा परीक्षा 2016 में <b>अखिल भारतीय रैंक 124</b> प्राप्त करके भारत की <b>प्रथम पूर्णतः दृष्टिबाधित महिला IAS अधिकारी</b> बनीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उनका <b>केरल कैडर</b> में नियुक्ति हुई और उन्होंने तिरुवनंतपुरम की उप-कलेक्टर तथा उल्हासनगर नगर निगम की CEO के रूप में कार्य किया।<br>• <b>बीनू ज़ेफ़ीन</b> <b>भारतीय विदेश सेवा</b> (2015) में जाने वाली प्रथम 100% दृष्टिबाधित महिला थीं, IAS में नहीं।<br>• <b>ईरा सिंघल</b> ने UPSC CSE 2014 में प्रथम स्थान पाया और वे दिव्यांग अधिकारी हैं, जबकि <b>किरण बेदी</b> भारत की प्रथम महिला IPS अधिकारी थीं।<br>• UPSC अपने परीक्षा नियमों के अंतर्गत दृष्टिबाधित अभ्यर्थियों को <b>लेखक तथा अतिरिक्त समय</b> की सुविधा देता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि प्रांजल पाटिल प्रथम पूर्णतः दृष्टिबाधित महिला IAS अधिकारी थीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000070324","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which State or Union Territory recorded the highest number of snow leopards according to the first nationwide Snow Leopard Population Assessment in India (SPAI), released on 30 January 2024? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"30 जनवरी 2024 को जारी भारत में प्रथम राष्ट्रव्यापी हिम तेंदुआ जनसंख्या आकलन (SPAI) के अनुसार किस राज्य या केंद्रशासित प्रदेश में सर्वाधिक हिम तेंदुए दर्ज हुए? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Himachal Pradesh","hi":"हिमाचल प्रदेश"},"2":{"en":"Sikkim","hi":"सिक्किम"},"3":{"en":"Jammu & Kashmir","hi":"जम्मू एवं कश्मीर"},"4":{"en":"Ladakh","hi":"लद्दाख"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Ladakh</b><br>According to the first nationwide <b>Snow Leopard Population Assessment in India (SPAI)</b> released on <b>30 January 2024</b>, India has an estimated <b>718 snow leopards</b>, and <b>Ladakh</b> recorded the highest number, about <b>477</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The assessment was carried out by the <b>Wildlife Institute of India</b> with the Snow Leopard Trust, Nature Conservation Foundation and state forest departments, covering over 70% of the species' range.<br>• After Ladakh, <b>Uttarakhand (124), Himachal Pradesh (51), Arunachal Pradesh (36), Sikkim (21) and Jammu and Kashmir (9)</b> reported snow leopards.<br>• The snow leopard (<b>Panthera uncia</b>) is listed as <b>Vulnerable</b> by IUCN, in Schedule I of the Wildlife Protection Act and Appendix I of CITES.<br>• The <b>Project Snow Leopard</b> and the climate, community and biodiversity benefits of its habitat make it an umbrella species of the high Himalayas.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because Ladakh recorded the highest number of snow leopards.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – लद्दाख</b><br><b>30 जनवरी 2024</b> को जारी प्रथम राष्ट्रव्यापी <b>भारत में हिम तेंदुआ जनसंख्या आकलन (SPAI)</b> के अनुसार भारत में लगभग <b>718 हिम तेंदुए</b> हैं और सर्वाधिक संख्या <b>लद्दाख</b> में लगभग <b>477</b> दर्ज हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह आकलन <b>वन्यजीव संस्थान, देहरादून</b> ने स्नो लेपर्ड ट्रस्ट, नेचर कंजर्वेशन फाउंडेशन तथा राज्य वन विभागों के साथ किया, जिसमें प्रजाति के आवास के 70% से अधिक भाग को सम्मिलित किया गया।<br>• लद्दाख के बाद <b>उत्तराखंड (124), हिमाचल प्रदेश (51), अरुणाचल प्रदेश (36), सिक्किम (21) तथा जम्मू-कश्मीर (9)</b> में हिम तेंदुए दर्ज हुए।<br>• हिम तेंदुआ (<b>Panthera uncia</b>) IUCN द्वारा <b>संवेदनशील (Vulnerable)</b>, वन्यजीव संरक्षण अधिनियम की अनुसूची I तथा CITES के परिशिष्ट I में सूचीबद्ध है।<br>• <b>प्रोजेक्ट स्नो लेपर्ड</b> तथा इसके आवास से मिलने वाले जलवायु, समुदाय एवं जैव विविधता लाभ इसे उच्च हिमालय की छत्र प्रजाति बनाते हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि लद्दाख में सर्वाधिक हिम तेंदुए दर्ज हुए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000070325","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Why is a reduction in public investment in social sectors considered a concern for economic development? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सामाजिक क्षेत्रों में सार्वजनिक निवेश में कमी को आर्थिक विकास के लिए चिंता का विषय क्यों माना जाता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Worsens inequities in education and healthcare","hi":"शिक्षा तथा स्वास्थ्य में असमानताएँ बढ़ जाती हैं"},"2":{"en":"Eliminates regional disparities and social inequalities","hi":"क्षेत्रीय विषमताएँ तथा सामाजिक असमानताएँ समाप्त हो जाती हैं"},"3":{"en":"Increases human capability and productivity automatically","hi":"मानव क्षमता तथा उत्पादकता स्वतः बढ़ जाती है"},"4":{"en":"Improves equality and access to services","hi":"समानता तथा सेवाओं तक पहुँच बेहतर हो जाती है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Worsens inequities in education and healthcare</b><br>A reduction in <b>public investment in social sectors</b> such as education and health <b>worsens inequities</b>, because the poor depend on public services while the rich can buy private services, which lowers human capital and long-run growth.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Social sector spending builds <b>human capital</b>, and its reduction hurts the quality of labour, productivity and future income.<br>• Public health and education are <b>merit goods</b> with positive externalities, so markets alone under-provide them.<br>• Reduced public spending shifts the burden to out-of-pocket private spending, worsening poverty and inequality.<br>• Options (2), (3) and (4) describe the opposite of what happens when public investment falls.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because lower social sector investment worsens inequities in education and healthcare.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – शिक्षा तथा स्वास्थ्य में असमानताएँ बढ़ जाती हैं</b><br>शिक्षा तथा स्वास्थ्य जैसे <b>सामाजिक क्षेत्रों में सार्वजनिक निवेश</b> की कमी <b>असमानताएँ बढ़ाती</b> है, क्योंकि गरीब सार्वजनिक सेवाओं पर निर्भर रहते हैं जबकि संपन्न निजी सेवाएँ खरीद सकते हैं, जिससे मानव पूँजी तथा दीर्घकालिक वृद्धि घटती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सामाजिक क्षेत्र का व्यय <b>मानव पूँजी</b> बनाता है और उसमें कमी श्रम की गुणवत्ता, उत्पादकता तथा भावी आय को हानि पहुँचाती है।<br>• सार्वजनिक स्वास्थ्य तथा शिक्षा <b>गुणवत्तापूर्ण वस्तुएँ (merit goods)</b> हैं जिनके सकारात्मक बाह्यताएँ हैं, इसलिए केवल बाजार उनकी पर्याप्त आपूर्ति नहीं करता।<br>• सार्वजनिक व्यय घटने पर भार निजी जेब-खर्च पर जाता है, जिससे गरीबी तथा असमानता बढ़ती है।<br>• विकल्प (2), (3) तथा (4) सार्वजनिक निवेश घटने पर होने वाले प्रभावों के विपरीत हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि सामाजिक क्षेत्र में कम निवेश शिक्षा तथा स्वास्थ्य की असमानताएँ बढ़ाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000070326","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"According to India's National Air Quality Index classification, which category corresponds to an Air Quality Index (AQI) range of 301–400? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के राष्ट्रीय वायु गुणवत्ता सूचकांक वर्गीकरण के अनुसार 301–400 की वायु गुणवत्ता सूचकांक (AQI) श्रेणी किसके अंतर्गत आती है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Severe","hi":"गंभीर (Severe)"},"2":{"en":"Moderate","hi":"मध्यम (Moderate)"},"3":{"en":"Very Poor","hi":"अत्यंत खराब (Very Poor)"},"4":{"en":"Poor","hi":"खराब (Poor)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Very Poor</b><br>In India's <b>National Air Quality Index</b>, the AQI range of <b>301–400</b> is classified as <b>'Very Poor'</b>, which triggers health warnings of respiratory illness on prolonged exposure.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The National AQI has six categories – <b>Good (0–50), Satisfactory (51–100), Moderate (101–200), Poor (201–300), Very Poor (301–400) and Severe (401–500)</b>.<br>• The index is computed from eight pollutants – <b>PM2.5, PM10, NO2, SO2, CO, O3, NH3 and Pb</b> – and the worst value determines the overall AQI.<br>• It was launched in <b>2014</b> by the Central Pollution Control Board under the Swachh Bharat Abhiyan.<br>• During 'Very Poor' air quality, the CPCB advises stopping outdoor activity, closing schools and using masks, and GRAP restrictions apply in Delhi-NCR.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because AQI 301–400 is categorised as Very Poor.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अत्यंत खराब (Very Poor)</b><br>भारत के <b>राष्ट्रीय वायु गुणवत्ता सूचकांक</b> में <b>301–400</b> की AQI श्रेणी <b>'अत्यंत खराब' (Very Poor)</b> कहलाती है, जो लंबे समय तक संपर्क में रहने पर श्वसन रोग की स्वास्थ्य चेतावनी देती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• राष्ट्रीय AQI की छह श्रेणियाँ हैं – <b>अच्छा (0–50), संतोषजनक (51–100), मध्यम (101–200), खराब (201–300), अत्यंत खराब (301–400) तथा गंभीर (401–500)</b>।<br>• सूचकांक आठ प्रदूषकों – <b>PM2.5, PM10, NO2, SO2, CO, O3, NH3 तथा Pb</b> – से निकाला जाता है, और सर्वाधिक खराब मान समग्र AQI निर्धारित करता है।<br>• इसे <b>2014</b> में केंद्रीय प्रदूषण नियंत्रण बोर्ड ने स्वच्छ भारत अभियान के अंतर्गत शुरू किया।<br>• 'अत्यंत खराब' वायु गुणवत्ता में CPCB बाहरी गतिविधि रोकने, विद्यालय बंद करने तथा मास्क के उपयोग की सलाह देता है, और दिल्ली-NCR में GRAP प्रतिबंध लागू होते हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि AQI 301–400 को अत्यंत खराब श्रेणी में रखा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000070327","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which of the following best describes the key feature of a Single Window System? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा एकल खिड़की प्रणाली (Single Window System) की प्रमुख विशेषता का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Providing integrated access to multiple approvals and clearances through a unified interface","hi":"एकीकृत इंटरफ़ेस के माध्यम से अनेक अनुमोदनों और मंजूरियों तक समेकित पहुँच प्रदान करना"},"2":{"en":"Requiring applicants to obtain clearances through separate departmental portals","hi":"आवेदकों से पृथक विभागीय पोर्टलों से मंजूरी लेने की अपेक्षा करना"},"3":{"en":"Transferring licensing functions from government agencies to private authorities","hi":"लाइसेंसिंग कार्यों को सरकारी एजेंसियों से निजी प्राधिकारियों को हस्तांतरित करना"},"4":{"en":"Requiring applicants to approach different departments independently for approvals","hi":"आवेदकों को स्वतंत्र रूप से विभिन्न विभागों के पास जाने की अपेक्षा करना"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Providing integrated access to multiple approvals and clearances through a unified interface</b><br>A <b>Single Window System</b> gives an investor <b>integrated access to multiple approvals and clearances through one unified interface</b>, so that separate visits to different departments are avoided.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Single window clearance reduces <b>compliance burden, time and cost of starting a business</b>, and is a key element of India's ease of doing business reforms.<br>• The <b>National Single Window System (NSWS)</b> portal, launched in 2021, allows investors to identify and apply for approvals from central and state departments in one place.<br>• State-level single window acts and industrial facilitation councils supplement the national portal.<br>• The system does not privatise licensing or require separate departmental applications, which is exactly what it replaces.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because a single window provides integrated access to multiple approvals.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – एकीकृत इंटरफ़ेस के माध्यम से अनेक अनुमोदनों और मंजूरियों तक समेकित पहुँच प्रदान करना</b><br><b>एकल खिड़की प्रणाली</b> निवेशक को <b>एक एकीकृत इंटरफ़ेस के माध्यम से अनेक अनुमोदनों तथा मंजूरियों तक समेकित पहुँच</b> देती है, जिससे विभिन्न विभागों में अलग-अलग चक्कर लगाने की आवश्यकता नहीं रहती।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• एकल खिड़की मंजूरी <b>अनुपालन का भार, समय तथा व्यवसाय शुरू करने की लागत</b> घटाती है और भारत के व्यवसाय सुगमता सुधारों का प्रमुख अंग है।<br>• 2021 में शुरू <b>राष्ट्रीय एकल खिड़की प्रणाली (NSWS)</b> पोर्टल निवेशकों को केंद्रीय एवं राज्य विभागों की मंजूरियाँ एक ही स्थान पर पहचानने तथा आवेदन करने देता है।<br>• राज्य-स्तरीय एकल खिड़की अधिनियम तथा औद्योगिक सुविधा परिषदें राष्ट्रीय पोर्टल की पूरक हैं।<br>• यह प्रणाली लाइसेंसिंग का निजीकरण नहीं करती और न ही पृथक विभागीय आवेदन चाहती है – वह इन्हीं का स्थान लेती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि एकल खिड़की अनेक अनुमोदनों तक समेकित पहुँच देती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000070328","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Reports and Indices (Current)","question":{"en":"In the World Happiness Report, what does the indicator “social support” measure? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"विश्व प्रसन्नता प्रतिवेदन में \"सामाजिक सहायता\" (social support) संकेतक किसका मापन करता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Whether a person has relatives or friends to count on in times of trouble","hi":"क्या किसी व्यक्ति के पास मुसीबत के समय भरोसा करने योग्य संबंधी या मित्र हैं"},"2":{"en":"The average size of a person’s family","hi":"किसी व्यक्ति के परिवार का औसत आकार"},"3":{"en":"The amount spent by the government on welfare programmes","hi":"कल्याणकारी कार्यक्रमों पर सरकार द्वारा किया गया व्यय"},"4":{"en":"The availability of assistance from non-governmental organizations","hi":"गैर-सरकारी संगठनों से सहायता की उपलब्धता"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Whether a person has relatives or friends to count on in times of trouble</b><br>In the <b>World Happiness Report</b>, 'social support' measures whether a person <b>has relatives or friends they can count on in times of trouble</b>, based on the Gallup World Poll question about having someone to rely on.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The report ranks countries on the <b>Cantril Ladder</b>, where respondents rate their current life on a 0-10 scale.<br>• The six explanatory factors are <b>GDP per capita, social support, healthy life expectancy, freedom to make life choices, generosity and perceptions of corruption</b>.<br>• It is published by the <b>Oxford Wellbeing Research Centre with Gallup and the UN SDSN</b>, and Finland has topped the ranking for several years.<br>• Family size, welfare spending and NGO assistance are not the components of this indicator.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because social support measures having someone to rely on in trouble.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – क्या किसी व्यक्ति के पास मुसीबत के समय भरोसा करने योग्य संबंधी या मित्र हैं</b><br><b>विश्व प्रसन्नता प्रतिवेदन</b> में 'सामाजिक सहायता' यह मापती है कि किसी व्यक्ति के पास <b>मुसीबत के समय भरोसा करने योग्य संबंधी या मित्र हैं या नहीं</b>, जो गैलप वर्ल्ड पोल के 'सहारे के लिए कोई हो' प्रश्न पर आधारित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रतिवेदन देशों को <b>कैंट्रिल लैडर</b> पर रैंक करता है, जिसमें उत्तरदाता अपने वर्तमान जीवन को 0-10 के पैमाने पर आँकते हैं।<br>• छह व्याख्यात्मक कारक हैं – <b>प्रति व्यक्ति GDP, सामाजिक सहायता, स्वस्थ जीवन प्रत्याशा, जीवन-चयन की स्वतंत्रता, उदारता तथा भ्रष्टाचार की धारणा</b>।<br>• यह <b>ऑक्सफोर्ड वेलबीइंग रिसर्च सेंटर द्वारा गैलप तथा UN SDSN के साथ</b> प्रकाशित होता है, और फिनलैंड कई वर्षों से शीर्ष पर है।<br>• परिवार का आकार, कल्याण व्यय तथा NGO सहायता इस संकेतक के घटक नहीं हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि सामाजिक सहायता मुसीबत में सहारे का मापन करती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000070329","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"Which statement best distinguishes ecosystem diversity from species diversity. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा कथन पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र विविधता तथा प्रजाति विविधता के बीच भेद का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ecosystem diversity measures aquatic habitats and water-based processes.","hi":"पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र विविधता जलीय आवासों तथा जल-आधारित प्रक्रियाओं का मापन करती है।"},"2":{"en":"Species diversity includes different species and their relative abundance.","hi":"प्रजाति विविधता में विभिन्न प्रजातियाँ तथा उनकी सापेक्ष बहुतायत सम्मिलित हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Ecosystem diversity includes varied habitats and ecological processes.","hi":"पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र विविधता में विविध आवास तथा पारिस्थितिकी प्रक्रियाएँ सम्मिलित हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Species diversity is unrelated to ecological interactions and ecosystem functions.","hi":"प्रजाति विविधता पारिस्थितिक अंतःक्रियाओं तथा पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र कार्यों से असंबंधित है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Ecosystem diversity includes varied habitats and ecological processes.</b><br><b>Ecosystem diversity</b> refers to the variety of <b>habitats, communities and ecological processes</b> in a region – forests, grasslands, wetlands, deserts and coral reefs – while species diversity refers to the variety of species and their relative abundance.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Biodiversity has three levels – <b>genetic diversity, species diversity and ecosystem diversity</b>.<br>• <b>Species richness</b> is the number of species and <b>species evenness</b> is their relative abundance; together they give species diversity.<br>• Ecosystem diversity is not limited to aquatic habitats (option 1 is too narrow), and species diversity is closely linked to ecological interactions (option 4 is wrong).<br>• India is a <b>megadiverse country</b> with 10 biogeographic zones and four biodiversity hotspots – the Himalayas, Western Ghats, Indo-Burma and Sundaland.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because ecosystem diversity includes varied habitats and ecological processes.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र विविधता में विविध आवास तथा पारिस्थितिकी प्रक्रियाएँ सम्मिलित हैं।</b><br><b>पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र विविधता</b> किसी क्षेत्र में <b>आवासों, समुदायों तथा पारिस्थितिकी प्रक्रियाओं</b> की विविधता है – वन, घासस्थल, आर्द्रभूमि, मरुस्थल तथा प्रवाल भित्तियाँ – जबकि प्रजाति विविधता प्रजातियों की विविधता तथा उनकी सापेक्ष बहुतायत को कहते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• जैव विविधता के तीन स्तर हैं – <b>आनुवंशिक विविधता, प्रजाति विविधता तथा पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र विविधता</b>।<br>• <b>प्रजाति समृद्धि</b> प्रजातियों की संख्या है और <b>प्रजाति समरूपता</b> उनकी सापेक्ष बहुतायत; दोनों मिलकर प्रजाति विविधता बनाते हैं।<br>• पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र विविधता केवल जलीय आवासों तक सीमित नहीं (विकल्प 1 संकीर्ण है), और प्रजाति विविधता पारिस्थितिक अंतःक्रियाओं से जुड़ी है (विकल्प 4 गलत है)।<br>• भारत <b>महाविविधता वाला देश</b> है, जहाँ 10 जैव-भौगोलिक क्षेत्र तथा चार जैव विविधता हॉटस्पॉट – हिमालय, पश्चिमी घाट, इंडो-बर्मा तथा सुंडालैंड – हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र विविधता में विविध आवास तथा पारिस्थितिकी प्रक्रियाएँ सम्मिलित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000070330","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"Which species is considered an indicator of healthy Indian grassland ecosystems? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सी प्रजाति भारतीय घासस्थल पारिस्थितिकी तंत्रों के स्वस्थ होने का संकेतक मानी जाती है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Indian bullfrog","hi":"भारतीय बुलफ्रॉग"},"2":{"en":"Great Indian bustard","hi":"ग्रेट इंडियन बस्टर्ड"},"3":{"en":"Olive Ridley turtle","hi":"ऑलिव रिडले कछुआ"},"4":{"en":"Rock python","hi":"रॉक पाइथन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Great Indian bustard</b><br>The <b>Great Indian bustard (Ardeotis nigriceps)</b> is considered an <b>indicator species of healthy Indian grassland ecosystems</b>, since it requires large, undisturbed, low-grazing grassland with scattered shrubs.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It is listed as <b>Critically Endangered</b> by IUCN, in Schedule I of the Wildlife Protection Act and Appendix I of CITES, and is the state bird of Rajasthan.<br>• Its main population survives in the <b>Desert National Park (Jaisalmer)</b> in Rajasthan, with smaller numbers in Gujarat and Maharashtra.<br>• Threats include <b>habitat loss, power-line collisions and free-ranging dogs</b>, and conservation breeding is carried out by the Wildlife Institute of India at Sam and Ramdevra.<br>• The <b>Indian bullfrog</b> is an amphibian, the <b>Olive Ridley turtle</b> is marine and the <b>rock python</b> is a large snake – none is a grassland indicator.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the Great Indian bustard indicates healthy Indian grasslands.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ग्रेट इंडियन बस्टर्ड</b><br><b>ग्रेट इंडियन बस्टर्ड (Ardeotis nigriceps)</b> को <b>स्वस्थ भारतीय घासस्थल पारिस्थितिकी तंत्रों की संकेतक प्रजाति</b> माना जाता है, क्योंकि इसके लिए विरल झाड़ियों वाले विशाल, अक्षत तथा कम-चराई वाले घासस्थल आवश्यक हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह IUCN द्वारा <b>गंभीर संकटग्रस्त (Critically Endangered)</b>, वन्यजीव संरक्षण अधिनियम की अनुसूची I तथा CITES के परिशिष्ट I में सूचीबद्ध है और राजस्थान का राज्य पक्षी है।<br>• इसकी मुख्य आबादी राजस्थान के <b>मरुस्थल राष्ट्रीय उद्यान (जैसलमेर)</b> में बची है, तथा गुजरात एवं महाराष्ट्र में कम संख्या है।<br>• संकटों में <b>आवास क्षति, विद्युत लाइनों से टकराव तथा आवारा कुत्ते</b> सम्मिलित हैं, और वन्यजीव संस्थान सैम तथा रामदेवरा में संरक्षण प्रजनन करता है।<br>• <b>भारतीय बुलफ्रॉग</b> उभयचर है, <b>ऑलिव रिडले कछुआ</b> समुद्री है तथा <b>रॉक पाइथन</b> बड़ा साँप है – इनमें से कोई घासस्थल का संकेतक नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि ग्रेट इंडियन बस्टर्ड स्वस्थ भारतीय घासस्थलों का संकेतक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000070331","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"Which of these is TRUE about the decimal expansion of √5? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"√5 के दशमलव प्रसार के बारे में निम्नलिखित में से क्या सत्य है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Terminating","hi":"सांत"},"2":{"en":"Repeating","hi":"आवर्ती"},"3":{"en":"Non-terminating, repeating","hi":"असांत, आवर्ती"},"4":{"en":"Non-terminating, non-repeating","hi":"असांत, अनावर्ती"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{5}\\) is an irrational number.<br>An irrational number has a decimal expansion that never ends and never repeats.<br>Hence it is \\(\\boxed{\\text{Non-terminating, non-repeating}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Non-terminating, non-repeating.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{5}\\) एक अपरिमेय संख्या है।<br>अपरिमेय संख्या का दशमलव प्रसार न समाप्त होता है और न ही दोहराता है।<br>अतः यह \\(\\boxed{\\text{असांत, अनावर्ती}}\\) है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): असांत, अनावर्ती है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000070332","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A pyramid has height 9 cm and base area 120 cm². If lateral surface area = 180 cm², what is total surface area? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक पिरामिड की ऊँचाई 9 cm और आधार का क्षेत्रफल 120 cm² है। यदि पार्श्व पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = 180 cm² है, तो कुल पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"180 cm³"},"2":{"en":"280 cm³"},"3":{"en":"240 cm³"},"4":{"en":"300 cm³"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Total surface area = base area + lateral surface area<br>\\(= 120 + 180 = \\boxed{300}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 300 cm³.</b>","hi":"कुल पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = आधार का क्षेत्रफल + पार्श्व पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल<br>\\(= 120 + 180 = \\boxed{300}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 300 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000070333","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Convert 210° to radians [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"210° को रेडियन में बदलिए [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7π/6"},"2":{"en":"5π/4"},"3":{"en":"11π/6"},"4":{"en":"3π/2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(210^\\circ = 210 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{7\\pi}{6}\\)<br>So the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{7\\pi}{6}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 7π/6.</b>","hi":"\\(210^\\circ = 210 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{7\\pi}{6}\\)<br>अतः उत्तर है \\(\\boxed{\\frac{7\\pi}{6}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 7π/6 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000070334","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"What must be added to each term of the ratio 5: 9 to make it equal to 2: 3? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अनुपात 5: 9 के प्रत्येक पद में क्या जोड़ा जाए कि वह 2: 3 के बराबर हो जाए? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6"},"2":{"en":"8"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let \\(x\\) be added: \\(\\frac{5 + x}{9 + x} = \\frac{2}{3}\\)<br>\\(15 + 3x = 18 + 2x\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए \\(x\\) जोड़ा जाता है: \\(\\frac{5 + x}{9 + x} = \\frac{2}{3}\\)<br>\\(15 + 3x = 18 + 2x\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000070335","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A sum of money becomes 3 times in 6 years at compound interest. Find the approximate annual rate of interest. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर कोई धनराशि 6 वर्षों में 3 गुनी हो जाती है। वार्षिक ब्याज दर लगभग ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10 %"},"2":{"en":"14 %"},"3":{"en":"17 %"},"4":{"en":"20 %"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(3P = P\\left(1 + \\frac{r}{100}\\right)^6 \\Rightarrow 1 + \\frac{r}{100} = 3^{1/6}\\)<br>\\(3^{1/6} = 1.2009\\)<br>\\(r \\approx 20\\%\\) per annum, i.e. \\(\\boxed{20\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 20 %.</b>","hi":"\\(3P = P\\left(1 + \\frac{r}{100}\\right)^6 \\Rightarrow 1 + \\frac{r}{100} = 3^{1/6}\\)<br>\\(3^{1/6} = 1.2009\\)<br>\\(r \\approx 20\\%\\) प्रति वर्ष, अर्थात् \\(\\boxed{20\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 20 % है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000070336","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A lighthouse is 180 m high. The angles of depression of two points are 45° and 60°. Find the approximate distance between the two points. (Use √3 = 1.732) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक प्रकाशस्तंभ 180 m ऊँचा है। दो बिंदुओं के अवनमन कोण 45° और 60° हैं। उन दोनों बिंदुओं के बीच की अनुमानित दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। (√3 = 1.732 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"67 m"},"2":{"en":"81 m"},"3":{"en":"76 m"},"4":{"en":"70 m"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Far point: \\(180\\cot 45^\\circ = 180\\) m<br>Near point: \\(180\\cot 60^\\circ = \\frac{180}{\\sqrt{3}} = 103.92\\) m<br>Distance = \\(180 - 103.92 = 76.08 \\approx \\boxed{76}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 76 m.</b>","hi":"दूर बिंदु: \\(180\\cot 45^\\circ = 180\\) m<br>निकट बिंदु: \\(180\\cot 60^\\circ = \\frac{180}{\\sqrt{3}} = 103.92\\) m<br>दूरी = \\(180 - 103.92 = 76.08 \\approx \\boxed{76}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 76 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000070337","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"The sides of a parallelogram are in the ratio of 5:4. Given that the sum of the squares of its diagonals is 328 cm², determine the length of the longer side. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक समांतर चतुर्भुज की भुजाएँ 5:4 के अनुपात में हैं। यदि उसके विकर्णों के वर्गों का योग 328 cm² है, तो लंबी भुजा की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 cm"},"2":{"en":"10 cm"},"3":{"en":"12 cm"},"4":{"en":"15 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"For a parallelogram, \\(d_1^2 + d_2^2 = 2(a^2 + b^2)\\)<br>Let the sides be \\(5x\\) and \\(4x\\):<br>\\(2(25x^2 + 16x^2) = 328 \\Rightarrow 82x^2 = 328 \\Rightarrow x^2 = 4 \\Rightarrow x = 2\\)<br>Longer side = \\(5 \\times 2 = \\boxed{10}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 10 cm.</b>","hi":"समांतर चतुर्भुज के लिए, \\(d_1^2 + d_2^2 = 2(a^2 + b^2)\\)<br>भुजाएँ \\(5x\\) और \\(4x\\) मानिए:<br>\\(2(25x^2 + 16x^2) = 328 \\Rightarrow 82x^2 = 328 \\Rightarrow x^2 = 4 \\Rightarrow x = 2\\)<br>लंबी भुजा = \\(5 \\times 2 = \\boxed{10}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 10 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000070338","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta = \\frac{7}{5}\\), find the value of \\(\\sin\\theta \\cdot \\cos\\theta\\). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta = \\frac{7}{5}\\) है, तो \\(\\sin\\theta \\cdot \\cos\\theta\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2}{25}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{13}{25}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{12}{25}\\)"},"4":{"en":"0"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Squaring: \\(\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta + 2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\frac{49}{25}\\)<br>\\(1 + 2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\frac{49}{25}\\)<br>\\(2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\frac{24}{25} \\Rightarrow \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\boxed{\\frac{12}{25}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{12}{25}\\).</b>","hi":"वर्ग करने पर: \\(\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta + 2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\frac{49}{25}\\)<br>\\(1 + 2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\frac{49}{25}\\)<br>\\(2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\frac{24}{25} \\Rightarrow \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\boxed{\\frac{12}{25}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{12}{25}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000070339","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3+z}+\\sqrt{3-z}}{\\sqrt{3+z}-\\sqrt{3-z}} = 2\\), then find the value of z. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3+z}+\\sqrt{3-z}}{\\sqrt{3+z}-\\sqrt{3-z}} = 2\\) है, तो z का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{14}{5}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{12}{5}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let \\(u = \\sqrt{3+z}\\), \\(v = \\sqrt{3-z}\\).<br>\\(\\frac{u+v}{u-v} = 2 \\Rightarrow u+v = 2u-2v \\Rightarrow \\frac{u}{v} = 3\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3+z}{3-z} = 9 \\Rightarrow 3 + z = 27 - 9z\\)<br>\\(10z = 24 \\Rightarrow z = \\boxed{\\frac{12}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{12}{5}\\).</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए \\(u = \\sqrt{3+z}\\), \\(v = \\sqrt{3-z}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{u+v}{u-v} = 2 \\Rightarrow u+v = 2u-2v \\Rightarrow \\frac{u}{v} = 3\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3+z}{3-z} = 9 \\Rightarrow 3 + z = 27 - 9z\\)<br>\\(10z = 24 \\Rightarrow z = \\boxed{\\frac{12}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{12}{5}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000070340","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{8+p}+\\sqrt{8-p}}{\\sqrt{8+p}-\\sqrt{8-p}} = 7\\), find the value of p. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{8+p}+\\sqrt{8-p}}{\\sqrt{8+p}-\\sqrt{8-p}} = 7\\) है, तो p का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{47}{56}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{56}{25}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let \\(u = \\sqrt{8+p}\\), \\(v = \\sqrt{8-p}\\).<br>\\(\\frac{u+v}{u-v} = 7 \\Rightarrow u+v = 7u-7v \\Rightarrow \\frac{u}{v} = \\frac{4}{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{8+p}{8-p} = \\frac{16}{9} \\Rightarrow 72 + 9p = 128 - 16p\\)<br>\\(25p = 56 \\Rightarrow p = \\boxed{\\frac{56}{25}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{56}{25}\\).</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए \\(u = \\sqrt{8+p}\\), \\(v = \\sqrt{8-p}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{u+v}{u-v} = 7 \\Rightarrow u+v = 7u-7v \\Rightarrow \\frac{u}{v} = \\frac{4}{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{8+p}{8-p} = \\frac{16}{9} \\Rightarrow 72 + 9p = 128 - 16p\\)<br>\\(25p = 56 \\Rightarrow p = \\boxed{\\frac{56}{25}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{56}{25}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000070341","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"If a chord of length 30 cm is drawn in a circle of radius 17 cm, what is the perpendicular distance from the center to the chord? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 17 cm त्रिज्या वाले वृत्त में 30 cm लंबी जीवा खींची जाए, तो केंद्र से जीवा तक की लंब दूरी क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4 cm"},"2":{"en":"8 cm"},"3":{"en":"12 cm"},"4":{"en":"15 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Half of the chord = \\(\\frac{30}{2} = 15\\) cm<br>Distance = \\(\\sqrt{17^2 - 15^2} = \\sqrt{289 - 225}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{64} = \\boxed{8}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 8 cm.</b>","hi":"जीवा का आधा = \\(\\frac{30}{2} = 15\\) cm<br>दूरी = \\(\\sqrt{17^2 - 15^2} = \\sqrt{289 - 225}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{64} = \\boxed{8}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 8 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000070342","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A hollow spherical metallic ball has an external diameter of 14 cm. If the thickness of the shell is 1 cm and the density of the metal is 8 g/cm³, find the total weight of the ball in kg. (Use π = 22/7) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक खोखली गोलाकार धातु की गेंद का बाहरी व्यास 14 cm है। यदि खोल की मोटाई 1 cm है और धातु का घनत्व 8 g/cm³ है, तो गेंद का कुल भार kg में ज्ञात कीजिए। (π = 22/7 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7.04 kg"},"2":{"en":"6.42 kg"},"3":{"en":"5.84 kg"},"4":{"en":"4.26 kg"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"External radius \\(R = 7\\) cm, internal radius \\(r = 6\\) cm<br>Volume of metal = \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi(R^3 - r^3) = \\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times (343 - 216)\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 127 = 532.19\\) cm³<br>Weight = \\(532.19 \\times 8 = 4257.5\\) g<br>\\(= \\boxed{4.26}\\) kg<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4.26 kg.</b>","hi":"बाहरी त्रिज्या \\(R = 7\\) cm, आंतरिक त्रिज्या \\(r = 6\\) cm<br>धातु का आयतन = \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi(R^3 - r^3) = \\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times (343 - 216)\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 127 = 532.19\\) cm³<br>भार = \\(532.19 \\times 8 = 4257.5\\) g<br>\\(= \\boxed{4.26}\\) kg<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 4.26 kg है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000070343","section":"MATH","topic":"Set Relation and Function","question":{"en":"In the real number system, the Archimedean property states: for any x ∈ R, there exists n ∈ N such that: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वास्तविक संख्या प्रणाली में, आर्किमिडीयन गुण बताता है: किसी भी x ∈ R के लिए, एक n ∈ N ऐसा होता है कि: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"n < x"},"2":{"en":"n > x"},"3":{"en":"n = x"},"4":{"en":"n ≤ x and n ≥ x simultaneously","hi":"एक साथ n ≤ x और n ≥ x"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The Archimedean property says that the natural numbers are unbounded above in R.<br>So for every real \\(x\\) there is a natural number bigger than it:<br>\\(\\boxed{n > x}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): n > x.</b>","hi":"आर्किमिडीयन गुण कहता है कि प्राकृत संख्याएँ R में ऊपर से असीमित हैं।<br>अतः प्रत्येक वास्तविक \\(x\\) के लिए उससे बड़ी कोई प्राकृत संख्या होती है:<br>\\(\\boxed{n > x}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): n > x है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000070344","section":"MATH","topic":"Set Relation and Function","question":{"en":"Let S = {x ∈ R : x² ∈ Q}. Which of the following best describes S? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मान लीजिए S = {x ∈ R : x² ∈ Q}। निम्नलिखित में से S का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"S = Q"},"2":{"en":"S is countable and properly contains Q","hi":"S गणनीय है और Q को उचित रूप से सम्मिलित करता है"},"3":{"en":"S = R"},"4":{"en":"S is a subfield of R","hi":"S, R का उपक्षेत्र है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(x^2 \\in \\mathbb{Q}\\) means \\(x\\) is a root of \\(X^2 - q\\) for some \\(q \\in \\mathbb{Q}\\), so \\(x\\) is algebraic of degree at most 2.<br>Such numbers are countable, and \\(\\mathbb{Q} \\subset S\\) properly because \\(\\sqrt{2} \\in S\\) but \\(\\sqrt{2} \\notin \\mathbb{Q}\\).<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{S \\text{ is countable and properly contains } \\mathbb{Q}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): S is countable and properly contains Q.</b>","hi":"\\(x^2 \\in \\mathbb{Q}\\) का अर्थ है कि \\(x\\) किसी \\(q \\in \\mathbb{Q}\\) के लिए \\(X^2 - q\\) का मूल है, अतः \\(x\\) अधिकतम घात 2 का बीजगणितीय है।<br>ऐसी संख्याएँ गणनीय हैं, और \\(\\mathbb{Q} \\subset S\\) उचित रूप से है क्योंकि \\(\\sqrt{2} \\in S\\) परंतु \\(\\sqrt{2} \\notin \\mathbb{Q}\\)।<br>अतः \\(\\boxed{S \\text{ गणनीय है और } \\mathbb{Q} \\text{ को उचित रूप से सम्मिलित करता है}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): S गणनीय है और Q को उचित रूप से सम्मिलित करता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000070345","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"The square of a positive number exceeds twice the number by 8. What is the number? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी धनात्मक संख्या का वर्ग उस संख्या के दोगुने से 8 अधिक है। वह संख्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"4"},"4":{"en":"6"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let the number be \\(x > 0\\): \\(x^2 = 2x + 8\\)<br>\\(x^2 - 2x - 8 = 0 \\Rightarrow (x - 4)(x + 2) = 0\\)<br>Taking the positive root, \\(x = \\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 4.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए संख्या \\(x > 0\\) है: \\(x^2 = 2x + 8\\)<br>\\(x^2 - 2x - 8 = 0 \\Rightarrow (x - 4)(x + 2) = 0\\)<br>धनात्मक मूल लेने पर, \\(x = \\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000070346","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A woman invested one-third of her savings at 8% simple interest for 6 years and the remaining amount at 10% simple interest for 4 years. At the end of the investment periods, the total simple interest earned from both investments was ₹18,240. Determine her total savings. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक महिला ने अपनी बचत का एक-तिहाई भाग 6 वर्षों के लिए 8% साधारण ब्याज पर और शेष राशि 4 वर्षों के लिए 10% साधारण ब्याज पर निवेश किया। निवेश अवधि के अंत में दोनों निवेशों से कुल साधारण ब्याज ₹18,240 प्राप्त हुआ। उसकी कुल बचत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹43,452"},"2":{"en":"₹42,750"},"3":{"en":"₹44,521"},"4":{"en":"₹45,100"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let the total savings be \\(x\\).<br>Interest 1 = \\(\\frac{x}{3} \\times \\frac{8 \\times 6}{100} = 0.16x\\)<br>Interest 2 = \\(\\frac{2x}{3} \\times \\frac{10 \\times 4}{100} = \\frac{0.8x}{3} = 0.2667x\\)<br>\\(0.4267x = 18240 \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{18240}{0.4267}\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{42{,}750}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹42,750.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए कुल बचत \\(x\\) है।<br>ब्याज 1 = \\(\\frac{x}{3} \\times \\frac{8 \\times 6}{100} = 0.16x\\)<br>ब्याज 2 = \\(\\frac{2x}{3} \\times \\frac{10 \\times 4}{100} = \\frac{0.8x}{3} = 0.2667x\\)<br>\\(0.4267x = 18240 \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{18240}{0.4267}\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{42{,}750}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹42,750 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000070347","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"Raunaq makes beautiful earthen vases and sells them. The price of each of these vases varies directly as the height, if they are of the same (material) thickness, and the price also varies directly as the square of the thickness if their heights are the same. A customer wants to buy two vases from Raunaq whose prices are in the ratio 28:81. If the ratio of the heights of these two vases is 16:7, respectively, find the ratio of their thicknesses. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रौनक़ सुंदर मिट्टी के फूलदान बनाकर बेचता है। यदि मोटाई (सामग्री की) समान हो तो प्रत्येक फूलदान का मूल्य ऊँचाई के सीधे समानुपाती होता है, और यदि ऊँचाई समान हो तो मूल्य मोटाई के वर्ग के सीधे समानुपाती होता है। एक ग्राहक रौनक़ से दो फूलदान खरीदना चाहता है जिनके मूल्य 28:81 के अनुपात में हैं। यदि इन दोनों फूलदानों की ऊँचाइयों का अनुपात क्रमशः 16:7 है, तो उनकी मोटाइयों का अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4:7"},"2":{"en":"4:9"},"3":{"en":"7:9"},"4":{"en":"7:18"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Price \\(\\propto\\) height × (thickness)²<br>\\(\\frac{28}{81} = \\frac{16}{7} \\times \\left(\\frac{t_1}{t_2}\\right)^2\\)<br>\\(\\left(\\frac{t_1}{t_2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{28 \\times 7}{81 \\times 16} = \\frac{196}{1296} = \\frac{49}{324}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{t_1}{t_2} = \\frac{7}{18}\\), i.e. \\(\\boxed{7:18}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 7:18.</b>","hi":"मूल्य \\(\\propto\\) ऊँचाई × (मोटाई)²<br>\\(\\frac{28}{81} = \\frac{16}{7} \\times \\left(\\frac{t_1}{t_2}\\right)^2\\)<br>\\(\\left(\\frac{t_1}{t_2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{28 \\times 7}{81 \\times 16} = \\frac{196}{1296} = \\frac{49}{324}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{t_1}{t_2} = \\frac{7}{18}\\), अर्थात् \\(\\boxed{7:18}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 7:18 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000070348","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"What is the value of \\(25\\sec^2\\theta - 25\\tan^2\\theta + 16\\csc^2\\theta - 16\\cot^2\\theta\\) for an acute angle θ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"न्यून कोण θ के लिए \\(25\\sec^2\\theta - 25\\tan^2\\theta + 16\\csc^2\\theta - 16\\cot^2\\theta\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"41"},"2":{"en":"49"},"3":{"en":"81"},"4":{"en":"20"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Group the terms: \\(25(\\sec^2\\theta - \\tan^2\\theta) + 16(\\csc^2\\theta - \\cot^2\\theta)\\)<br>Using the identities, each bracket equals 1:<br>\\(= 25 + 16 = \\boxed{41}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 41.</b>","hi":"पदों को समूहित कीजिए: \\(25(\\sec^2\\theta - \\tan^2\\theta) + 16(\\csc^2\\theta - \\cot^2\\theta)\\)<br>सर्वसमिकाओं का उपयोग करने पर प्रत्येक कोष्ठक 1 के बराबर है:<br>\\(= 25 + 16 = \\boxed{41}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 41 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000070349","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"How many solutions does the equation sinθ = 1/2 have for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 90°? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"समीकरण sinθ = 1/2 के 0° ≤ θ ≤ 90° के लिए कितने हल हैं? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the interval \\(0^\\circ \\le \\theta \\le 90^\\circ\\), \\(\\sin\\theta\\) increases steadily from 0 to 1.<br>So \\(\\sin\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\) occurs exactly once, at \\(\\theta = 30^\\circ\\).<br>Number of solutions = \\(\\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"अंतराल \\(0^\\circ \\le \\theta \\le 90^\\circ\\) में \\(\\sin\\theta\\) 0 से 1 तक लगातार बढ़ता है।<br>अतः \\(\\sin\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\) ठीक एक बार होता है, \\(\\theta = 30^\\circ\\) पर।<br>हलों की संख्या = \\(\\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000070350","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Evaluate: \\(\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos(90^\\circ-\\theta)} + \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin(90^\\circ-\\theta)}\\) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मूल्यांकन कीजिए: \\(\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos(90^\\circ-\\theta)} + \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin(90^\\circ-\\theta)}\\) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"−2"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"−1"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\cos(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\sin\\theta\\) and \\(\\sin(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\cos\\theta\\)<br>Expression = \\(\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} + \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\)<br>\\(= 1 + 1 = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2.</b>","hi":"\\(\\cos(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\sin\\theta\\) और \\(\\sin(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\cos\\theta\\)<br>व्यंजक = \\(\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} + \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\)<br>\\(= 1 + 1 = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000070351","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If p + q + r = 12 and pq + qr + rp = 47, what is the value of p² + q² + r²? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि p + q + r = 12 और pq + qr + rp = 47 है, तो p² + q² + r² का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"44"},"2":{"en":"46"},"3":{"en":"48"},"4":{"en":"50"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\((p + q + r)^2 = p^2 + q^2 + r^2 + 2(pq + qr + rp)\\)<br>\\(144 = p^2 + q^2 + r^2 + 94\\)<br>\\(p^2 + q^2 + r^2 = \\boxed{50}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 50.</b>","hi":"\\((p + q + r)^2 = p^2 + q^2 + r^2 + 2(pq + qr + rp)\\)<br>\\(144 = p^2 + q^2 + r^2 + 94\\)<br>\\(p^2 + q^2 + r^2 = \\boxed{50}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 50 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000070352","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"If the length of a tangent from an external point to a circle is 24 cm and the radius of the circle is 7 cm, then the distance from the center to the external point is: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि किसी बाह्य बिंदु से वृत्त पर खींची गई स्पर्श रेखा की लंबाई 24 cm है और वृत्त की त्रिज्या 7 cm है, तो केंद्र से बाह्य बिंदु तक की दूरी है: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"19 cm"},"2":{"en":"21 cm"},"3":{"en":"23 cm"},"4":{"en":"25 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The radius is perpendicular to the tangent at the point of contact, so the triangle is right-angled.<br>\\(d^2 = r^2 + t^2 = 7^2 + 24^2 = 49 + 576 = 625\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{25}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 25 cm.</b>","hi":"स्पर्श बिंदु पर त्रिज्या स्पर्श रेखा के लंबवत होती है, अतः त्रिभुज समकोणीय है।<br>\\(d^2 = r^2 + t^2 = 7^2 + 24^2 = 49 + 576 = 625\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{25}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 25 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000070353","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In an equilateral triangle ABC with a side length of 8 units, point D is the midpoint of side BC. A line passing through D is parallel to side AC and intersects side AB at point E. Find the length of segment DE. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"8 इकाई भुजा वाले समबाहु त्रिभुज ABC में, बिंदु D भुजा BC का मध्यबिंदु है। D से होकर भुजा AC के समांतर एक रेखा खींची जाती है जो भुजा AB को बिंदु E पर मिलती है। रेखाखंड DE की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2 units","hi":"2 इकाई"},"2":{"en":"3 units","hi":"3 इकाई"},"3":{"en":"4 units","hi":"4 इकाई"},"4":{"en":"6 units","hi":"6 इकाई"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Since \\(DE \\parallel AC\\) and D is the midpoint of BC, E is the midpoint of AB (midpoint theorem).<br>So DE joins the midpoints of two sides and equals half the third side:<br>\\(DE = \\frac{AC}{2} = \\frac{8}{2} = \\boxed{4}\\) units<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 4 units.</b>","hi":"चूँकि \\(DE \\parallel AC\\) और D, BC का मध्यबिंदु है, अतः E, AB का मध्यबिंदु है (मध्यबिंदु प्रमेय)।<br>अतः DE दो भुजाओं के मध्यबिंदुओं को मिलाता है और तीसरी भुजा की आधी होती है:<br>\\(DE = \\frac{AC}{2} = \\frac{8}{2} = \\boxed{4}\\) इकाई<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 4 इकाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000070354","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A line is tangent to two distinct coplanar circles C₁ and C₂. This line is called a: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक रेखा दो भिन्न समतलीय वृत्तों C₁ और C₂ की स्पर्श रेखा है। इस रेखा को कहते हैं: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Common secant","hi":"उभयनिष्ठ छेदक"},"2":{"en":"Common chord","hi":"उभयनिष्ठ जीवा"},"3":{"en":"Common tangent","hi":"उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा"},"4":{"en":"Radical axis","hi":"मूल अक्ष"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A line touching both circles (touching each at exactly one point) is, by definition, a common tangent of the two circles.<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{\\text{Common tangent}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Common tangent.</b>","hi":"दोनों वृत्तों को (प्रत्येक को ठीक एक बिंदु पर) स्पर्श करने वाली रेखा परिभाषा से दोनों वृत्तों की उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा होती है।<br>अतः \\(\\boxed{\\text{उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000070355","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A, B, C and D can complete a work individually in 20 days, 25 days, 40 days and 50 days, respectively. All four work together for 2 days. Then A, B and C continue for 3 more days. Next A and B work for 4 days. Finally C returns at 150% of his original efficiency and D returns at twice his original efficiency; C and D together finish the remaining work. If ₹31,000 is divided according to actual work done, what is C's share? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A, B, C और D किसी कार्य को अलग-अलग क्रमशः 20 दिन, 25 दिन, 40 दिन और 50 दिन में पूरा कर सकते हैं। चारों मिलकर 2 दिन कार्य करते हैं। फिर A, B और C 3 दिन और कार्य करते हैं। इसके बाद A और B 4 दिन कार्य करते हैं। अंत में C अपनी मूल क्षमता के 150% पर और D अपनी मूल क्षमता के दोगुने पर लौटते हैं; C और D मिलकर शेष कार्य पूरा करते हैं। यदि ₹31,000 वास्तविक किए गए कार्य के अनुसार बाँटा जाए, तो C का हिस्सा क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹3,950"},"2":{"en":"₹4,100"},"3":{"en":"₹4,250"},"4":{"en":"₹4,400"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Rates: A = \\(\\frac{1}{20}\\), B = \\(\\frac{1}{25}\\), C = \\(\\frac{1}{40}\\), D = \\(\\frac{1}{50}\\); together = \\(\\frac{10+8+5+4}{200} = \\frac{27}{200}\\)<br>First 2 days (all four): \\(\\frac{54}{200}\\)<br>Next 3 days (A, B, C): \\(3 \\times \\frac{23}{200} = \\frac{69}{200}\\)<br>Next 4 days (A, B): \\(4 \\times \\frac{18}{200} = \\frac{72}{200}\\)<br>Work left = \\(1 - \\frac{195}{200} = \\frac{5}{200}\\)<br>Final rates: C = \\(\\frac{1.5}{40} = \\frac{7.5}{200}\\), D = \\(\\frac{2}{50} = \\frac{8}{200}\\); together \\(\\frac{15.5}{200}\\) → time = \\(\\frac{5}{15.5}\\) days<br>C's total work = \\(\\frac{10}{200} + \\frac{15}{200} + \\frac{5}{15.5} \\times \\frac{7.5}{200} = 0.05 + 0.075 + 0.0121 = 0.1371\\)<br>C's share = ₹\\(0.1371 \\times 31{,}000 = \\boxed{4{,}250}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹4,250.</b>","hi":"दरें: A = \\(\\frac{1}{20}\\), B = \\(\\frac{1}{25}\\), C = \\(\\frac{1}{40}\\), D = \\(\\frac{1}{50}\\); मिलकर = \\(\\frac{10+8+5+4}{200} = \\frac{27}{200}\\)<br>पहले 2 दिन (चारों): \\(\\frac{54}{200}\\)<br>अगले 3 दिन (A, B, C): \\(3 \\times \\frac{23}{200} = \\frac{69}{200}\\)<br>अगले 4 दिन (A, B): \\(4 \\times \\frac{18}{200} = \\frac{72}{200}\\)<br>शेष कार्य = \\(1 - \\frac{195}{200} = \\frac{5}{200}\\)<br>अंतिम दरें: C = \\(\\frac{1.5}{40} = \\frac{7.5}{200}\\), D = \\(\\frac{2}{50} = \\frac{8}{200}\\); मिलकर \\(\\frac{15.5}{200}\\) → समय = \\(\\frac{5}{15.5}\\) दिन<br>C का कुल कार्य = \\(\\frac{10}{200} + \\frac{15}{200} + \\frac{5}{15.5} \\times \\frac{7.5}{200} = 0.05 + 0.075 + 0.0121 = 0.1371\\)<br>C का हिस्सा = ₹\\(0.1371 \\times 31{,}000 = \\boxed{4{,}250}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹4,250 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000070356","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Convert the below given indirect speech into direct speech appropriately:<br>He told her that he had finished his homework. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He told her, “I finish my homework”."},"2":{"en":"He told her, “He have finished his homework”."},"3":{"en":"He told her, “I finished my homework”."},"4":{"en":"He told her, “He had finished his homework”."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Reported past perfect can return to simple past in the direct statement.</b><br>The speaker becomes “I,” and “his homework” becomes “my homework.”<br>“I finished my homework” is the keyed direct form.<br>The other options retain reporting forms or lack agreement.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): He told her, “I finished my homework”..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000070357","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) during the festival season<br>B) traffic congestion<br>C) is a common sight<br>D) in metropolitan cities [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"C-B-D-A"},"2":{"en":"A-B-C-D"},"3":{"en":"D-A-B-C"},"4":{"en":"B-D-A-C"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: A-B-C-D</b><br>A establishes the time: during the festival season.<br>B and C state that traffic congestion is common.<br>D identifies the setting: metropolitan cities.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A-B-C-D.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000070358","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) under the Beti Bachao Beti Padhao scheme<br>B) improvement in gender ratio<br>C) several districts<br>D) have shown [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"C-D-B-A"},"2":{"en":"D-B-C-A"},"3":{"en":"A-B-C-D"},"4":{"en":"B-D-C-A"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: C-D-B-A</b><br>C and D form the subject and verb: several districts have shown.<br>B states the improvement in gender ratio.<br>A names the scheme under which it occurred.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): C-D-B-A.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000070359","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correct preposition:<br>The Prime Minister emphasised the importance of digital literacy ___ rural women to bridge the digital divide. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"after"},"2":{"en":"with"},"3":{"en":"across"},"4":{"en":"among"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Among (के बीच) = within a group.</b><br>Digital literacy is to be promoted among rural women.<br>“After” indicates time, “with” accompaniment, and “across” a span or movement.<br>Only “among” identifies the target population.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): among.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000070360","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Spot the error in the following sentence and identify the INCORRECT part.<br>Each of the players <b>were awarded</b> a certificate of appreciation. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Each of the players"},"2":{"en":"were awarded"},"3":{"en":"a certificate of appreciation"},"4":{"en":"No error"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Each of + plural noun” takes a singular verb.</b><br>The head word is “each,” so use “was awarded.”<br>Correct sentence: “Each of the players <b>was awarded</b> a certificate.”<br>The erroneous phrase is “were awarded.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): were awarded.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000070361","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>In recent years, India has witnessed a steady rise in the number of self-help groups (SHGs), particularly among rural women. These groups, usually comprising 10-20 women, function as collectives that provide mutual support and financial interdependence. Most SHGs are involved in small-scale economic activities such as tailoring, pickling, and handicrafts, and many receive support from government schemes and microfinance institutions. The objective is not only economic empowerment but also social inclusion. SHGs often become platforms for discussing issues such as health, sanitation, and gender equality. In states like Tamil Nadu and Odisha, SHGs have played a crucial role in community-level decision-making, especially during crises like the COVID-19 pandemic. However, challenges like limited market access and lack of digital literacy continue to impede their growth. With the right support, SHGs could become powerful agents of transformation in India's rural landscape.<br><br><br>What is the primary objective of Self-Help Groups (SHGs) as mentioned in the passage? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Economic empowerment and social inclusion"},"2":{"en":"Ensuring social media access"},"3":{"en":"Providing loans to large-scale industries"},"4":{"en":"Promoting tourism in rural areas"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: The objective is not only economic empowerment but also social inclusion.</b><br>SHGs combine financial cooperation with discussion of social issues.<br>Social media, large industries and tourism are not their stated aims.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Economic empowerment and social inclusion.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000070362","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>In recent years, India has witnessed a steady rise in the number of self-help groups (SHGs), particularly among rural women. These groups, usually comprising 10-20 women, function as collectives that provide mutual support and financial interdependence. Most SHGs are involved in small-scale economic activities such as tailoring, pickling, and handicrafts, and many receive support from government schemes and microfinance institutions. The objective is not only economic empowerment but also social inclusion. SHGs often become platforms for discussing issues such as health, sanitation, and gender equality. In states like Tamil Nadu and Odisha, SHGs have played a crucial role in community-level decision-making, especially during crises like the COVID-19 pandemic. However, challenges like limited market access and lack of digital literacy continue to impede their growth. With the right support, SHGs could become powerful agents of transformation in India's rural landscape.<br><br><br>According to the passage, how many women typically form an SHG? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-5"},"2":{"en":"10-20"},"3":{"en":"50-100"},"4":{"en":"30-40"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: The groups usually comprise 10–20 women.</b><br>They function as small collectives for mutual support.<br>The other numerical ranges are not stated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 10-20.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000070363","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>In recent years, India has witnessed a steady rise in the number of self-help groups (SHGs), particularly among rural women. These groups, usually comprising 10-20 women, function as collectives that provide mutual support and financial interdependence. Most SHGs are involved in small-scale economic activities such as tailoring, pickling, and handicrafts, and many receive support from government schemes and microfinance institutions. The objective is not only economic empowerment but also social inclusion. SHGs often become platforms for discussing issues such as health, sanitation, and gender equality. In states like Tamil Nadu and Odisha, SHGs have played a crucial role in community-level decision-making, especially during crises like the COVID-19 pandemic. However, challenges like limited market access and lack of digital literacy continue to impede their growth. With the right support, SHGs could become powerful agents of transformation in India's rural landscape.<br><br><br>In which areas have SHGs contributed besides economic activities? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only infrastructure development"},"2":{"en":"Political campaigning"},"3":{"en":"Social issues like health and sanitation"},"4":{"en":"Tax policy changes"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: SHGs discuss health, sanitation and gender equality.</b><br>They therefore contribute to social as well as economic development.<br>Infrastructure, campaigning and tax policy are not mentioned.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Social issues like health and sanitation.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000070364","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>In recent years, India has witnessed a steady rise in the number of self-help groups (SHGs), particularly among rural women. These groups, usually comprising 10-20 women, function as collectives that provide mutual support and financial interdependence. Most SHGs are involved in small-scale economic activities such as tailoring, pickling, and handicrafts, and many receive support from government schemes and microfinance institutions. The objective is not only economic empowerment but also social inclusion. SHGs often become platforms for discussing issues such as health, sanitation, and gender equality. In states like Tamil Nadu and Odisha, SHGs have played a crucial role in community-level decision-making, especially during crises like the COVID-19 pandemic. However, challenges like limited market access and lack of digital literacy continue to impede their growth. With the right support, SHGs could become powerful agents of transformation in India's rural landscape.<br><br><br>What major challenge faced by SHGs is highlighted in the passage? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Excessive government regulation"},"2":{"en":"Overstaffing"},"3":{"en":"High taxation"},"4":{"en":"Lack of digital literacy and market access"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Limited market access and lack of digital literacy impede growth.</b><br>These are the two major challenges highlighted.<br>Regulation, staffing and taxation are not discussed.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Lack of digital literacy and market access.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000070365","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>In recent years, India has witnessed a steady rise in the number of self-help groups (SHGs), particularly among rural women. These groups, usually comprising 10-20 women, function as collectives that provide mutual support and financial interdependence. Most SHGs are involved in small-scale economic activities such as tailoring, pickling, and handicrafts, and many receive support from government schemes and microfinance institutions. The objective is not only economic empowerment but also social inclusion. SHGs often become platforms for discussing issues such as health, sanitation, and gender equality. In states like Tamil Nadu and Odisha, SHGs have played a crucial role in community-level decision-making, especially during crises like the COVID-19 pandemic. However, challenges like limited market access and lack of digital literacy continue to impede their growth. With the right support, SHGs could become powerful agents of transformation in India's rural landscape.<br><br><br>How did SHGs contribute during the COVID-19 pandemic, as per the passage? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They offered community-level decision-making"},"2":{"en":"They moved operations online"},"3":{"en":"They distributed vaccines door-to-door"},"4":{"en":"They suspended all activities"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: SHGs played a crucial role in community-level decision-making during crises.</b><br>The pandemic is given as an example.<br>Online migration, vaccine delivery and suspension are not mentioned.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): They offered community-level decision-making.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000070366","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Clutch at straws” [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Attempt desperately"},"2":{"en":"Handle fragile objects"},"3":{"en":"Succeed against odds"},"4":{"en":"Refuse to help"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Clutch at straws (हर संभव हailाकलाप करना) = try anything in desperation.</b><br>Example: “He was clutching at straws to save the failing project.”<br>It does not mean handling objects or actually succeeding.<br>Refusal to help is unrelated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Attempt desperately.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000070367","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Choose the correctly spelt word that best completes the sentence meaningfully.<br>The ___ of the new software update includes several useful features. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"fuctionality"},"2":{"en":"functinality"},"3":{"en":"functionality"},"4":{"en":"functionallity"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Functionality (कार्यक्षमता) = the range of operations something can perform.</b><br>The correct spelling is “functionality.”<br><b>Fuctionality</b> omits “n”; <b>functinality</b> omits “o.”<br><b>Functionallity</b> doubles “l.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): functionality.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000070368","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>The manager had left (1)/ before the team arrives (2)/ causing confusion (3)/ about the agenda. (4) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The past perfect “had left” requires a later simple-past reference.</b><br>Part (2) should read “before the team <b>arrived</b>.”<br>“Arrives” incorrectly shifts into the present.<br>The remaining parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): (2).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000070369","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Identify the appropriate one-word substitution for:<br>A person who is indifferent to pain or pleasure. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Stoic"},"2":{"en":"Pessimist"},"3":{"en":"Optimist"},"4":{"en":"Narcissist"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Stoic (स्थिरचित्त) = one who remains unmoved by pleasure or pain.</b><br><b>Pessimist (निराशावादी)</b> = expects bad outcomes<br><b>Optimist (आशावादी)</b> = expects good outcomes<br><b>Narcissist (आत्ममुग्ध)</b> = excessively self-absorbed person<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Stoic.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000070370","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “To go the extra mile” mean? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To put in extra effort to achieve something"},"2":{"en":"To work just enough to get by"},"3":{"en":"To avoid working on something"},"4":{"en":"To do something with less effort"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Go the extra mile (अतिरिक्त प्रयास करना) = make a special additional effort.</b><br>Example: “She went the extra mile to help her clients.”<br>Minimal work, avoidance and reduced effort are opposite ideas.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): To put in extra effort to achieve something.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000070371","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “To have a sweet tooth” mean? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To enjoy spicy foods"},"2":{"en":"To dislike sugary foods"},"3":{"en":"To have a liking for sweet foods"},"4":{"en":"To prefer savoury foods"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Have a sweet tooth (मीठा पसंद करना) = like sweet foods.</b><br>Example: “I have a sweet tooth, so I love desserts.”<br>Spicy and savoury preferences are different.<br>Disliking sugar is the opposite.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): To have a liking for sweet foods.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000070372","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the correct spelling of the word used to describe someone who serves the nation, especially in the army. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Soldier"},"2":{"en":"Soldiar"},"3":{"en":"Souldier"},"4":{"en":"Soulier"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Soldier (सैनिक) = a member of an army.</b><br>The correct spelling is “soldier.”<br><b>Soldiar</b> reverses the ending; <b>souldier</b> inserts “u.”<br><b>Soulier</b> omits “d.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Soldier.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000070373","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence:<br>The changes were subtle yet <b>profoundly impacted the outcome</b>. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"impacted profoundly"},"2":{"en":"had profound impact on"},"3":{"en":"profound impacting"},"4":{"en":"profoundly impacting"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Have an impact on” is the standard noun construction.</b><br>Correct wording: “yet <b>had a profound impact on</b> the outcome” in its compact keyed form.<br>The adjective “profound” modifies “impact.”<br>The other options use incorrect or less natural structures.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): had profound impact on.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000070374","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence:<br>They congratulated him <b>for</b> his promotion. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"at his promotion"},"2":{"en":"on his promotion"},"3":{"en":"of his promotion"},"4":{"en":"over his promotion"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Congratulate someone on something” is standard.</b><br>Correct sentence: “They congratulated him <b>on</b> his promotion.”<br>“At,” “of” and “over” do not fit this construction.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): on his promotion.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000070375","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>Critics had long questioned the validity of the experimental model. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The validity of the experimental model was being questioned."},"2":{"en":"The validity of the experimental model had long been questioned by critics."},"3":{"en":"The model's validity was long questioned by critics."},"4":{"en":"The validity had been being questioned for long."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past perfect passive = had been + past participle.</b><br>The object “validity” becomes the subject, and “long” is retained before “been.”<br>“By critics” identifies the agent.<br>The other options change the aspect or phrasing.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The validity of the experimental model had long been questioned by critics..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000070376","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>They must have completed the construction by the time the inspection happens. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The construction must have been completed by the time of the inspection."},"2":{"en":"The construction is completed by inspection time."},"3":{"en":"The construction was to be completed for inspection."},"4":{"en":"The construction must have completed by the time of inspection."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Modal perfect passive = modal + have been + past participle.</b><br>“Must have completed” becomes “must have been completed.”<br>The construction becomes the subject.<br>The other options alter the modal perfect form.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The construction must have been completed by the time of the inspection..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000070377","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>The officer enquired, in a tone of suppressed irritation, why the requisition requests had been repeatedly submitted with incomplete documentation. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“Why do you keep submitting incomplete requisitions?” asked the officer."},"2":{"en":"“Don't submit requisitions without documentation.”"},"3":{"en":"“Why have the requisition forms repeatedly lacked complete documentation?” he asked irritably."},"4":{"en":"“Why were the requisitions submitted incomplete each time?” the officer asked."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Restore the direct question and the officer’s irritated tone.</b><br>C asks why the forms repeatedly lacked complete documentation and includes “irritably.”<br>A omits the tone; B changes the question into a command.<br>D retains an unnecessarily past-oriented question.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): “Why have the requisition forms repeatedly lacked complete documentation?” he asked irritably..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000070378","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. The package is labelled and handed over to the delivery service.<br>2. The items are carefully packed using protective materials.<br>3. A confirmation is sent to the buyer with tracking details.<br>4. The payment is verified before packaging. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4-2-1-3"},"2":{"en":"1-2-4-3"},"3":{"en":"4-1-2-3"},"4":{"en":"2-4-1-3"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 4-2-1-3</b><br>Payment is verified, and then the items are packed.<br>The package is labelled and handed to delivery.<br>Tracking confirmation is sent last.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 4-2-1-3.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000070379","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “A person who studies and deciphers ancient inscriptions”. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Philologist"},"2":{"en":"Lexicographer"},"3":{"en":"Epigrapher"},"4":{"en":"Numismatist"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Epigrapher (शिलालेख-विशेषज्ञ) = one who studies inscriptions.</b><br><b>Philologist (भाषाविद)</b> = studies language and texts<br><b>Lexicographer (कोशकार)</b> = compiles dictionaries<br><b>Numismatist (मुद्राशास्त्री)</b> = studies coins<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Epigrapher.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000070380","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"In this question, the closing fragment of a sentence is fixed and labelled as S5. The remainder of the sentence has been split into four parts—P, Q, R, S—which are not in the proper order. Rearrange these parts to form the most grammatically and logically coherent sentence ending with S5. Choose the correct sequence from the options provided.<br>P: simultaneously charged with triangular grains of starch, I observed some Actinophorous rhizopods creeping about them that had similar shaped<br>Q: on one occasion, while investigating the nature of some large, transparent, spore-like elliptical cells whose protoplasm was rotating while being<br>R: grains of starch in their interior, and after determining the nature of these grains by the addition of iodine, I cleansed the glasses and placed under the<br>S: microscope a new portion of the sediment from the basin containing these cells and Actinophryans for further examination, at which point I observed<br>S5: that one of the spore-like cells had become ruptured and that a portion of its protoplasm, charged with the triangular starch grains, was slightly protruding through the crevice. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SRQP"},"2":{"en":"QPRS"},"3":{"en":"RQPS"},"4":{"en":"PRSQ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QPRS</b><br>Q introduces the investigation and the rotating protoplasm.<br>P continues with the triangular grains and rhizopods.<br>R and S describe iodine testing and microscopic re-examination, leading to S5.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): QPRS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};